WEBVTT

00:41.960 --> 00:48.000
<i>Around the Earth float hundreds
of gigantic space colonies.</i>

00:48.000 --> 00:53.650
<i>For fifty years, mankind has made his
home within their cylindrical walls.</i>

00:53.650 --> 00:57.130
<i>Half of humanity
are now space colonists.</i>

00:57.130 --> 01:01.300
<i>The year is U.C. 0079.</i>

01:07.380 --> 01:10.310
<i>The colonies of Side 3, have declared
themselves the Principality of Zeon...</i>

01:10.310 --> 01:14.970
<i>...and launched a war of independence
against the Earth Federation.</i>

01:14.970 --> 01:17.170
<i>The first month of
fighting saw each side lose...</i>

01:17.170 --> 01:18.880
<i>...half of their
respective populations.</i>

01:18.880 --> 01:23.390
<i>All of mankind was horrified by
the atrocities it committed.</i>

01:34.180 --> 01:36.310
<i>Amuro Ray,
a young pilot on the White Base...</i>

01:36.310 --> 01:40.400
<i>...the new Earth Federal Forces warship...</i>

01:40.400 --> 01:46.200
<i>...has grown into an experienced
soldier through numerous battles.</i>

01:49.690 --> 01:57.530
<i>And, as the war took a new turn,
the White Base launched back into space.</i>

01:57.530 --> 02:03.800
<i>But their bitter enemy,
Char Aznable, was close behind.</i>

02:47.980 --> 02:51.410
<i>Minovsky particle broadcast
is at full combat density!</i>

02:51.410 --> 02:53.640
<i>All hands, prepare
for ship-to-ship combat!</i>

02:54.190 --> 02:56.920
Confirmed. One ship in pursuit!

02:57.330 --> 02:59.110
Chen's coming!

02:59.110 --> 03:01.740
Char, the Red Comet?

03:01.740 --> 03:04.390
No doubt about it.
It's definitely him.

03:04.800 --> 03:06.360
How do you know?

03:06.360 --> 03:08.330
I... It's just...

03:08.330 --> 03:10.920
Sayla! Stand by
in the Core-Booster!

03:10.920 --> 03:11.860
Aye, sir.

03:11.860 --> 03:16.000
Ensign Mirai, accelerate towards
point E-300, as planned.

03:16.200 --> 03:18.570
Aye, sir. If we do that...

03:18.570 --> 03:22.240
...it should look like the
White Base is headed for moon.

03:22.650 --> 03:24.970
Do you suppose Sayla's a Newtype?

03:26.760 --> 03:29.100
Do Newtypes have
precognition as well?

03:29.760 --> 03:31.260
Maybe not.

03:32.760 --> 03:38.480
Mind if I tag along? We're both
Core-Booster pilots, after all.

03:45.610 --> 03:46.450
Well?

03:47.780 --> 03:49.840
This is the Trojan Horse's
projected course.

03:49.840 --> 03:51.670
It looks like it's headed for the moon.

03:51.670 --> 03:54.710
The moon?! They're going after
Lady Kycilia's Granada Base?

03:54.710 --> 03:56.340
Doubtful.

03:57.190 --> 04:00.540
It's a trick.
The Trojan Horse is a decoy.

04:00.540 --> 04:04.130
Their main fleet is probably
launching from Jaburo as we speak.

04:04.130 --> 04:06.010
Then we should change course!

04:06.230 --> 04:08.920
Are you serious?
If we turn our backs...

04:08.920 --> 04:10.650
...the Trojan Horse will attack us.

04:10.650 --> 04:12.470
Do we have any
ships in this area?

04:12.470 --> 04:15.150
The Camel Patrol Fleet
should be nearby.

04:15.150 --> 04:16.290
Can we contact them?

04:16.290 --> 04:19.460
Aye, sir. I've been
tracing their course.

04:19.460 --> 04:21.020
- Hail them.
- Aye, sir.

04:22.940 --> 04:26.270
<i>Lieutenant Dren! It's
Captain Char on the Zanzibar!</i>

04:26.270 --> 04:29.570
<i>Oh! Captain,
it's been too long.</i>

04:29.570 --> 04:33.550
You're looking well, Dren.
I need your help again.

04:33.550 --> 04:35.560
<i>If there's anything I can do, sir...</i>

04:35.560 --> 04:40.920
We're after the Trojan Horse.
Your fleet's in position to out them off.

04:41.100 --> 04:43.230
<i>You just can't get free of that thing,
can you?</i>

04:43.230 --> 04:44.260
Combat alert 1!

04:44.260 --> 04:46.630
<i>Understood, sir.
Can you catch up with them?</i>

04:46.630 --> 04:50.030
Who do you think
you're talking to, Dren?

04:50.030 --> 04:52.190
<i>Sorry, sir.</i>

04:52.190 --> 04:55.240
Being back out in
space seems to suit you.

04:55.240 --> 04:56.530
<i>Is that flattery?</i>

04:58.080 --> 05:01.380
Change course! Minus 110!

05:14.450 --> 05:16.820
All units, confirm
catapult launch track!

05:16.820 --> 05:20.260
Maintenance personnel, take shelter
at once! One minute to launch!

05:20.260 --> 05:22.210
I'm expecting some ass-kicking
from you, Ensign Kai!

05:22.210 --> 05:24.420
Sure! Leave it to me!

05:27.920 --> 05:30.840
C-109, standing by to launch!

05:37.290 --> 05:40.100
Amuro, Gundam: catapult stand by!

05:40.560 --> 05:42.150
Space...

05:43.230 --> 05:45.150
Amuro, moving out!

05:50.400 --> 05:53.160
<i>006! 005! Ready for launch!</i>

05:56.440 --> 06:00.090
<i>Won't you resign from the
Federal Forces, Artesia?</i>

06:00.090 --> 06:03.170
<i>Sayla! Are you there? Answer me!</i>

06:03.710 --> 06:04.750
<i>Understand?</i>

06:05.910 --> 06:08.130
<i>006, launch!</i>

06:08.130 --> 06:10.090
Sayla, 006, moving out!

06:13.120 --> 06:14.590
Your #2 engine's
running a little roughly.

06:15.160 --> 06:17.550
I told you I understood that, right?

06:17.550 --> 06:19.420
Now get back before
you get blown outta here!

06:19.420 --> 06:20.820
Sleggar, moving out!

06:20.820 --> 06:23.690
Sir, please get into a normal suit!

06:23.690 --> 06:27.070
Idiot, a commander never
gets into a normal suit first!

06:27.740 --> 06:30.090
The last thing I need is
to scare my men.

06:30.090 --> 06:31.780
All units, full combat speed!

06:40.820 --> 06:43.670
The Camel Fleet will contact
the Trojan Horse in 30 seconds.

06:43.670 --> 06:44.970
We're 3 minutes behind them.

06:44.970 --> 06:50.220
Excellent. We'll close with the
Camel fleet and support them.

06:51.290 --> 06:52.950
<i>Artesia...</i>

06:53.430 --> 06:58.090
<i>She was wearing a Federal Forces
uniform when I saw her.</i>

06:58.470 --> 07:01.720
<i>Artesia, who I thought hated
fighting more than anyone.</i>

07:04.270 --> 07:08.010
There's no way she'd ever
get on a battleship again.

07:08.010 --> 07:12.020
Right! Go to combat
alert 1! Move it!

07:12.020 --> 07:16.210
I'm not one to
follow a lady's lead.

07:18.790 --> 07:19.870
Let's give it a try!

07:21.590 --> 07:24.220
Sleggar? Too soon, man!
Too soon!

07:28.600 --> 07:30.980
At times like this,
haste'll get you wasted!

07:32.590 --> 07:34.490
They're splitting off
to the left and right!

07:34.490 --> 07:37.550
Hayato! Sayla!
Lieutenant Sleggar! Go low!

07:46.350 --> 07:47.100
Incoming!

07:50.650 --> 07:51.400
Damn!

07:53.660 --> 07:54.900
Sloppy, Kai!

07:58.990 --> 07:59.740
Perfect!

08:05.870 --> 08:08.830
White Base, do you read?
We're turning to give support.

08:11.810 --> 08:13.660
I'll leave the evasive
action to you, Mirai.

08:13.660 --> 08:15.210
Aye, sir!

08:18.310 --> 08:19.640
Hard to starboard!

08:27.690 --> 08:29.480
Direct hit! The left-flank Musai!

08:31.430 --> 08:35.400
Pull those two Rick-Doms back!
They're blocking our fire!

08:35.400 --> 08:37.450
The Camel and the Swamel
will cut the Trojan Horse off!

08:41.000 --> 08:42.190
The white one from the Trojan Horse...

08:42.190 --> 08:43.950
What?! I didn't hear you!

08:43.950 --> 08:46.310
They don't see
the Gundam out there!

08:46.310 --> 08:47.870
Who's in that Rick-Dom?

08:47.870 --> 08:52.110
Fraci, sir. He says he
doesn't see the Gundam.

08:52.480 --> 08:55.440
Then where is it?

08:57.450 --> 09:01.550
No, it has to be out there.
But where?!

09:01.550 --> 09:02.550
Lieutenant Dren!

09:02.550 --> 09:03.260
What?!

09:03.260 --> 09:05.640
Object approaching at 12 o'clock!

09:05.860 --> 09:07.080
What?!

09:07.080 --> 09:10.830
It looks like a mobile suit...
Heat sources, closing fast!

09:10.830 --> 09:11.890
Missiles?!

09:11.890 --> 09:13.860
They're not headed
for this ship, sir!

09:14.400 --> 09:15.480
The Swamel?!

09:21.810 --> 09:26.300
<i>The Gundam...</i>
That <i>white monster...</i>

09:53.110 --> 09:54.030
Excellent!

09:54.030 --> 09:55.640
All enemy vessels
destroyed, sir!

09:55.640 --> 09:57.770
What about that ship on our tail?

09:57.770 --> 10:01.170
They'll be within effective
firing range in 30 seconds, sir!

10:01.850 --> 10:02.950
What do you think, Mirai?

10:03.120 --> 10:07.150
Oh? Once he sees
how well we're fighting...

10:07.150 --> 10:09.440
...he won't close to attack.

10:09.790 --> 10:11.620
Chen's like that.

10:12.160 --> 10:14.460
Yes. I agree.

10:14.930 --> 10:18.060
Aft missiles,
lay down a cover barrage!

10:18.060 --> 10:22.000
Mobile suits and Core-Boosters
will fall in behind us in a Y-line.

10:22.000 --> 10:25.300
Maintain course at full speed!
Get us out of this sector!

10:31.010 --> 10:32.270
Good work.

10:32.270 --> 10:33.710
Excellent as always, Amuro.

10:33.710 --> 10:35.940
Hey, Newtype! Newtype!

10:35.940 --> 10:40.040
So, is the plan to go to Solomon?
Or maybe to Granada?

10:40.040 --> 10:41.240
I can't say that now.

10:41.240 --> 10:44.360
But, to buy us some time,
we'll head to Side 6.

10:45.790 --> 10:46.570
Side 6, sir?

10:47.530 --> 10:50.290
It's to provide a decoy
for the next operation.

10:50.290 --> 10:53.920
Side 6 is neutral,
<i>so</i> we can't fight there.

10:53.920 --> 10:57.660
Unfortunately, we need to go so
they don't guess what our plans are.

10:57.660 --> 11:01.240
If we do,
they could surround us.

11:01.240 --> 11:04.310
So, that means we're more or less
on leave till the next operation.

11:04.310 --> 11:05.640
Well, you could always
get some more time...

11:05.640 --> 11:08.340
...in the Core-Booster
simulator, Lieutenant.

11:09.250 --> 11:10.930
Is there a problem, Mirai?

11:10.930 --> 11:16.910
N- No, sir. White Base,
setting course for Side 6.

11:17.360 --> 11:18.440
Very well, then.

11:18.440 --> 11:23.310
<i>Oh, right. You have a
fiancé. Sorry about that.</i>

11:23.310 --> 11:25.240
<i>No, it's...</i>

11:25.870 --> 11:29.000
<i>All that “fiancé" talk is
just because of our parents.</i>

11:29.000 --> 11:30.430
<i>Where is he?</i>

11:30.430 --> 11:33.620
<i>He ran off to Side 6
to avoid the war.</i>

11:34.810 --> 11:37.330
<i>If we weren't ordered to,
I wouldn't take us there!</i>

11:38.950 --> 11:42.550
<i>This is the sector
which once contained Side 1.</i>

11:42.550 --> 11:47.580
<i>It is now the site of Solomon,
the base of operations of...</i>

11:47.580 --> 11:49.300
<i>...the Zeon space assault corps,</i>

11:50.190 --> 11:53.650
<i>Its commander,
Vice Admiral Dozle Zabi...</i>

11:53.650 --> 11:56.920
<i>...wished to show his sister,
Kycilia, that Captain Char...</i>

11:56.920 --> 12:01.940
<i>whom she recruited after Dozle
discharged him, was incompetent.</i>

12:01.940 --> 12:05.070
<i>But, as he didn't know
the objectives of...</i>

12:05.070 --> 12:09.490
<i>...the Federal Force fleet
gathering at Luna H .</i>

12:09.490 --> 12:14.540
<i>...he could only afford to dispatch the Conscon Fleet.</i>

12:19.620 --> 12:24.020
<i>Meanwhile, the White Base,
with Char still in pursuit...</i>

12:24.020 --> 12:29.310
<i>...has entered the airspace of
the neutral colonies of Side 6.</i>

12:42.340 --> 12:43.490
Welcome aboard.

12:43.490 --> 12:45.370
I'm Cameron Bloom,

12:45.370 --> 12:46.820
the Immigration Bureau
Inspector of Side 6.

12:53.120 --> 12:55.310
We've placed these
seals over all of...

12:55.310 --> 12:58.620
...the White Base's missile ports,
cannons, and beam cannons.

12:58.620 --> 13:00.310
If even one is broken...

13:00.310 --> 13:03.950
I know. We have
to pay a stiff fine.

13:03.950 --> 13:04.990
Exactly.

13:04.990 --> 13:07.240
To what extent
can we resupply here?

13:07.240 --> 13:10.380
I'm afraid you
can't do that in Side 6.

13:10.380 --> 13:13.930
We cannot allow any
war-related cooperation.

13:14.210 --> 13:15.390
I'll show you to the bridge.

13:16.710 --> 13:19.700
Ah, we're just in
time for the docking.

13:20.380 --> 13:23.060
White Base, now docking.
Stand by for mooring.

13:27.020 --> 13:30.940
360 degree
laser sensors, open!

13:33.460 --> 13:36.290
Mirai! Mirai, is it you?!

13:36.290 --> 13:37.700
Cameron! You!

13:38.270 --> 13:42.080
Mirai, you're alive! Mirai...

13:43.300 --> 13:44.960
You're looking well, too.

13:47.010 --> 13:48.100
<i>Who's that?</i>

13:48.100 --> 13:49.090
Maybe he's a relative.

13:50.280 --> 13:54.930
Inspector Cameron, we're docking!
Please control yourself!

13:54.930 --> 13:55.640
And you, Ensign Mirai.

13:55.640 --> 13:59.640
Yes, Lieutenant. Forgive me.

13:59.640 --> 14:01.110
Mirai...

14:24.110 --> 14:29.840
I'm so happy! I'd given up all
hope of ever seeing you again.

14:29.840 --> 14:31.880
It's all this war's fault.

14:31.880 --> 14:35.080
If your father hadn't died,
maybe it wouldn't have happened.

14:35.080 --> 14:41.280
You're right. I might not
have emigrated to Side 7.

14:41.280 --> 14:45.560
But why didn't you tell
me where you were, Mirai?!

14:45.560 --> 14:48.190
I was desperate for
any news about you!

14:48.190 --> 14:48.990
Desperate?

14:48.990 --> 14:51.360
Yes! I had my men search for
you as hard as they could.

14:51.360 --> 14:53.530
I don't know how
much money I spent!

14:53.710 --> 14:55.230
Really...

14:56.980 --> 15:00.760
Why didn't you
look for me yourself?

15:00.760 --> 15:03.850
It happened just when
I emigrated to Side 6.

15:03.850 --> 15:07.710
So, our engagement really was just
something our parents arranged...

15:07.710 --> 15:10.410
That's not true, Mirai!
You've got me all wrong!

15:10.410 --> 15:12.420
Come on, let's talk this over.

15:12.420 --> 15:15.320
Won't you come with me?
Father will be so happy to see you.

15:15.320 --> 15:16.460
But...

15:16.460 --> 15:20.590
You can't think so badly of me,
Mirai! I'd do anything for you!

15:20.590 --> 15:22.770
Now, just wait a minute!

15:22.770 --> 15:24.490
Excuse me.

15:28.410 --> 15:30.160
I suggest you leave
the ensign alone, pal.

15:30.160 --> 15:33.190
Lieutenant Sleggar,
it's all right!

15:33.440 --> 15:34.970
You're sure?

15:34.970 --> 15:36.180
Yes.

15:37.080 --> 15:41.970
If she says so, Mr. Gentleman.
Here, your glasses.

15:43.160 --> 15:44.880
Cameron, are you all right?

15:44.880 --> 15:49.710
Yes. I may be trying too hard
to win you back. Right, Lieutenant?

15:50.460 --> 15:52.030
You could say that.

15:52.030 --> 15:56.270
Remember, we consider Ensign Mirai
to be the White Base's mother.

15:56.270 --> 15:59.260
Did you get your money
exchanged, Lieutenant Tamura?

15:59.260 --> 16:00.630
Yeah, I'm fine.

16:00.630 --> 16:02.100
We're moving!

16:03.380 --> 16:09.880
<i>The space colony's central block
maintains a state of zero gravity.</i>

16:09.880 --> 16:13.240
<i>As the elevator carries them
3000 meters down to...</i>

16:13.240 --> 16:17.530
<i>...the artificial land below,
the feeling of weight returns.</i>

16:19.230 --> 16:22.950
<i>There, a warm,
Earth-like landscape,</i> ,,

16:22.950 --> 16:26.960
<i>...with mountains, forests,
and cities, has been constructed.</i>

16:30.380 --> 16:32.430
Wow, cool!

16:32.430 --> 16:34.670
It'll be nice to have
something different for a change.

16:34.840 --> 16:37.470
Will they send
the rest by tomorrow?

16:37.470 --> 16:39.760
They should.
I told them to hurry.

16:44.220 --> 16:45.020
<i>Dad...</i>

16:47.390 --> 16:48.880
What's wrong, Amuro?

16:48.880 --> 16:49.980
Go back without me!

16:50.690 --> 16:51.480
Hey!

16:51.480 --> 16:52.810
Sorry!

17:06.170 --> 17:07.860
Dad!

17:07.860 --> 17:08.620
What them?!

17:28.760 --> 17:29.690
Dad!

17:31.330 --> 17:33.300
Oh, Amuro.

17:33.300 --> 17:35.010
Dad!

17:35.010 --> 17:38.070
So, how's the Gundam working?
Running well?

17:39.440 --> 17:41.550
Yes, Dad.

17:41.550 --> 17:42.910
Come with me.

17:42.910 --> 17:44.070
Yes, sir.

17:48.120 --> 17:51.170
What's the matter?
Come in! Come in!

17:53.990 --> 17:55.610
<i>What' s...?</i>

17:56.190 --> 18:00.050
A junkyard's a great place
for picking up information.

18:00.960 --> 18:03.940
That's why I live here.

18:03.940 --> 18:07.660
Install this in the
Gundam's memory system.

18:07.660 --> 18:10.700
I based it on a Zeon
mobile suit design.

18:10.700 --> 18:12.760
<i>It's a piece of junk,</i> ,,

18:13.240 --> 18:16.690
<i>Dad... Do you have oxygen
deprivation syndrome?</i>

18:17.350 --> 18:21.580
It's great! It'll increase its
combat ability by several orders!

18:21.580 --> 18:25.440
Here, take it!
And install it soon!

18:25.440 --> 18:27.950
Sure...
What about you, Dad?

18:27.950 --> 18:30.540
I'm in the middle of
a lot of research now.

18:30.540 --> 18:33.380
I'll contact you later.
Now get going!

18:39.170 --> 18:43.120
Dad, I saw Mom back home...

18:44.670 --> 18:49.010
Dad... Don't you even
care about her anymore?

18:49.010 --> 18:51.670
Of course. This war
will be over soon.

18:51.670 --> 18:54.100
Once it is,
we'll go back to Earth.

18:55.020 --> 18:56.270
<i>Dad...</i>

18:56.920 --> 18:59.730
Go! Aren't you a soldier now?!

19:25.310 --> 19:26.700
Welcome back.

19:26.700 --> 19:27.710
Thanks.

19:27.710 --> 19:29.380
They don't want us?

19:29.380 --> 19:31.810
They're looking for an
excuse to get us deported.

19:31.810 --> 19:34.890
The war's about
to come to a head...

19:34.890 --> 19:37.820
<i>...so</i> the Side 6
government's getting nervous.

19:37.820 --> 19:39.400
Here.

19:39.400 --> 19:40.540
Is this mine?

19:40.540 --> 19:43.000
I didn't trust your
orderly to do it right.

19:43.000 --> 19:44.510
<i>Thanks...</i>

19:44.510 --> 19:47.910
So, there's a problem with
our being in pod here?

19:48.740 --> 19:53.430
Yes. The Zabi family has
influence in Side 6's assembly.

19:54.340 --> 19:56.790
Thanks again.
Not going ashore?

19:57.610 --> 19:59.100
Probably not.

19:59.580 --> 20:03.370
You talked with Cameron?

20:03.370 --> 20:04.670
He's so wrong.

20:05.390 --> 20:11.530
He thinks the war isn't his
concern. I can't stand it.

20:11.530 --> 20:13.180
Really...

20:13.830 --> 20:16.480
You should protect your
relationships with others, though.

20:17.730 --> 20:18.850
You really mean that?

20:22.570 --> 20:27.430
I try to live my life as
cleverly as other people <i>do...</i>

20:27.430 --> 20:29.400
...but I can be <i>so</i> clumsy.

20:32.110 --> 20:33.740
Yes, you are.

20:45.830 --> 20:50.250
Damn it! They should have
given us the weather schedule!

21:24.060 --> 21:25.890
<i>Poor thing...</i>

21:38.180 --> 21:39.200
<i>Poor thing...</i>

22:22.790 --> 22:25.880
Pardon me.
I don't mean to disturb you.

22:25.880 --> 22:30.630
Was it that bird that
you were admiring?

22:30.630 --> 22:34.330
Is there anyone who doesn't
like a beautiful thing?

22:35.270 --> 22:38.030
I was thinking
how sad it was...

22:38.030 --> 22:40.700
...that it would
grow old and die someday.

22:40.700 --> 22:43.540
Didn't you feel
anything like that?

22:43.540 --> 22:50.500
Uh, no. That's not
what I was asking.

22:51.170 --> 22:52.680
It's clearing!

23:01.600 --> 23:03.230
You've very pretty eyes.

23:04.600 --> 23:05.520
You think so?

23:39.900 --> 23:44.360
Really? I'm so happy!
You're the Gundam's pilot!

23:44.360 --> 23:46.480
So, how did that module
I gave you last night work?

23:47.370 --> 23:51.450
Come on!
The new pan I gave you!

23:51.450 --> 23:56.480
The improvement was incredible!
Wasn't it? Wasn't it, Amuro?!

23:56.480 --> 23:58.410
Yeah, well...

23:58.410 --> 24:03.440
Yes, of course it worked!
Wonderful, it works!

24:03.440 --> 24:06.870
Now I can concentrate on
developing new inventions.

24:07.030 --> 24:14.130
Yes, it works perfectly.
Right, because I made it.

24:14.130 --> 24:17.030
No one knows the
Gundam as well as I do.

24:17.030 --> 24:20.300
<i>Goodbye, Dad...</i>

24:32.090 --> 24:33.680
<i>Dad! Do you really
think these mobile suits...</i>

24:33.680 --> 24:36.010
<i>...are more important
than peoples' lives?!</i>

24:36.010 --> 24:37.210
<i>Let's go!</i>

24:37.210 --> 24:38.640
<i>Dad!</i>

24:38.640 --> 24:40.410
<i>Get to the White Base!</i>

24:40.410 --> 24:41.690
<i>White Base...?</i>

24:43.800 --> 24:46.060
Oh, great!

25:15.100 --> 25:16.520
<i>Char!</i>

25:17.630 --> 25:22.430
Sorry, kid.
My driver's still new at this.

25:22.970 --> 25:24.200
Did we splash you?

25:24.770 --> 25:27.700
Uh, no!
I was able to dodge it.

25:27.890 --> 25:31.360
Sorry. I guess
I was going too fast.

25:31.360 --> 25:32.400
Not at all!

25:32.400 --> 25:34.730
We'll have to tow
it out with our car...

25:35.050 --> 25:36.940
Lalah, open the trunk, would you?

25:36.940 --> 25:37.670
Yes, sir!

25:37.670 --> 25:40.110
- If you'd give me a hand...
- My name's Amuro Ray, sir!

25:40.550 --> 25:43.650
Amuro Ray? Amuro...

25:43.960 --> 25:47.290
Strange, I seem to know
that name from somewhere.

25:48.760 --> 25:54.230
<i>Yeah, you know me. And I know you.</i>

26:01.240 --> 26:03.160
<i>Lalah, huh?</i>

26:07.680 --> 26:10.940
Please, let me help.

26:10.940 --> 26:13.720
Relax. I'm done.

26:13.720 --> 26:17.220
Thanks, really.
Um, what's your name?

26:17.220 --> 26:20.670
Char Aznable. As you
can see, I'm a soldier.

26:20.670 --> 26:21.790
<i>Char!</i>

26:21.790 --> 26:24.450
Lalah, move the
car forward slowly.

26:24.450 --> 26:25.930
Yes, Captain.

26:25.930 --> 26:29.890
<i>That's Char. Char Aznable.</i>

26:33.870 --> 26:35.940
What's wrong? Stand back, Amuro.

26:37.180 --> 26:41.840
<i>I only just met him now.
Why did I know he was Char?</i>

26:41.840 --> 26:45.650
<i>And that girl... “Lalah"...</i>

26:56.360 --> 26:58.850
How old are you?

26:59.400 --> 27:00.710
Si- Sixteen, sir!

27:00.710 --> 27:03.020
Really. Pretty young.

27:03.020 --> 27:05.730
I know you're nervous about
being near an enemy officer...

27:05.730 --> 27:09.130
...but I was hoping
you'd at least thank me.

27:09.510 --> 27:10.270
Let me get that!

27:15.080 --> 27:16.340
Thank you very much, sir.

27:16.340 --> 27:20.110
No problem. Too bad I wasn't
the only one who got dirty.

27:20.890 --> 27:22.850
That's okay...

27:22.850 --> 27:27.370
Really!
Th- Thank you very much!

27:32.330 --> 27:34.890
What's his problem?

27:36.200 --> 27:37.920
He was scared.

27:37.920 --> 27:41.570
He knows that you're
the great Red Comet, Char.

27:50.650 --> 27:52.410
There's nothing we can do about it.

27:52.410 --> 27:57.350
If they say we have to go into
battle, we have to leave Side 6.

27:57.350 --> 27:59.410
But a fleet's waiting for us!

27:59.410 --> 28:02.820
Captain! Inspector
Cameron is here for you.

28:02.820 --> 28:05.860
Right. I heard you. Bring him in.

28:05.860 --> 28:07.240
Aye, sir.

28:07.240 --> 28:10.940
Cameron, is this about our leaving?

28:10.940 --> 28:13.860
The fleet waiting for you
is the Conscon Fleet.

28:13.860 --> 28:16.000
It's under Vice Admiral Dozle.

28:16.680 --> 28:21.710
They may attack you while you're
still inside Side 6's airspace.

28:21.710 --> 28:26.910
At least let me escort you
while you're inside the perimeter.

28:26.910 --> 28:30.680
I have my private launch with me,
so I can act as your shield.

28:30.680 --> 28:31.950
I'd appreciate it.

28:31.950 --> 28:35.050
Cameron! What do you
think you're doing?!

28:35.660 --> 28:38.930
How can you talk that way?!

28:39.330 --> 28:41.460
I don't want you
interfering with this!

28:41.460 --> 28:44.030
It's none of
your business, right?!

28:44.030 --> 28:47.500
Mirai... If you won't get off
this ship, then I should at least...

28:47.500 --> 28:49.410
This is exactly what
I was talking about!

28:50.010 --> 28:52.730
Mirai, that isn't fair!

28:52.730 --> 28:55.830
You're just doing this to
try to look good!

28:55.830 --> 28:57.540
I would never be that petty!

28:57.540 --> 28:58.870
- This is my fault!

28:58.870 --> 29:02.210
You weren't there when I
needed you the most, and now...I

29:02.210 --> 29:06.850
I'm trying to make it up to you.

29:07.360 --> 29:09.010
I want you to understand how I feel.

29:09.010 --> 29:09.990
No, thank you!

29:09.990 --> 29:13.320
Mirai! I'd never try to
force you into anything...

29:18.840 --> 29:20.400
Lieutenant!

29:20.810 --> 29:23.600
This guy's on the level!
Can't you see that?

29:23.600 --> 29:25.600
If he wasn't, you think
he'd be carrying on like this?!

29:25.600 --> 29:27.870
Even if we are
in Side 6's airspace...

29:27.870 --> 29:30.200
...one stray missile
could kill him!

29:30.750 --> 29:35.320
And you! Why do you let
her bust your ass like that?

29:35.320 --> 29:36.710
Well, I wouldn't have hit her!

29:36.710 --> 29:38.220
If you meant what you said,
you would have!

29:38.220 --> 29:40.610
But, it's barbaric.

29:41.560 --> 29:44.920
Right, Cameron. It's your
personality that's the problem here.

29:44.920 --> 29:46.460
Right, Ensign?

29:46.460 --> 29:48.170
How could you...!

29:48.170 --> 29:49.970
Sorry, sorry.

29:53.840 --> 29:58.340
If you haven't changed your mind,
will you still do it, Cameron?

29:58.340 --> 29:59.980
What? Oh, yes.

30:00.170 --> 30:01.390
All right, Ensign?

30:03.650 --> 30:05.110
As you wish, Captain.

30:05.650 --> 30:08.030
Hey! Welcome back, Newtype!

30:08.860 --> 30:09.640
What happened?

30:09.640 --> 30:11.820
Nothing that concerns you.

30:13.390 --> 30:15.020
I appreciate your help.

30:15.020 --> 30:17.330
No problem.
Well, I'll see you later.

30:43.890 --> 30:45.560
A signal flare
from Kayahawa?

30:45.780 --> 30:48.290
The Trojan Horse is
leaving Side 6's airspace.

30:48.290 --> 30:50.420
Confirm its position!
Engines to full!

30:51.870 --> 30:54.790
Don't go thinking you can
join your main fleet unharmed!

30:54.790 --> 30:55.830
They're trying to escape in...

30:55.830 --> 30:57.580
...the opposite direction
at full combat speed!

30:58.170 --> 31:02.660
We won't let them!
Launch all Rick-Dams!

31:03.410 --> 31:06.670
Move it! I don't care
if we violate their airspace!

31:06.670 --> 31:10.210
Either way, once they leave the
area, they'll have to fight us!

31:16.720 --> 31:19.480
All hands, hold your fire while
we're still in Side 6's perimeter.

31:19.480 --> 31:21.520
Is that clear? Do not
fire even if fired upon!

31:25.770 --> 31:28.690
You've got some nerve,
you skirt-wearing freaks!

31:33.820 --> 31:38.070
This wasn't part of the deal!
I expect a big bonus for this!

31:38.070 --> 31:39.450
Fine!

31:40.050 --> 31:41.470
Here they come!

31:42.620 --> 31:44.370
Make no move until they do!

31:47.150 --> 31:51.340
Cameron, we're almost to the
perimeter. If we don't go back...

31:51.340 --> 31:52.590
<i>I know...</i>

31:56.300 --> 31:58.340
Here they come!

31:58.340 --> 32:00.930
Get the kids into normal suits.

32:00.930 --> 32:03.360
<i>Bright, those Zeon mobile suits...</i>

32:03.360 --> 32:06.230
I know. You've come far enough.

32:06.230 --> 32:08.770
We'll go to full combat speed
and try to break out of here.

32:08.770 --> 32:10.770
<i>No, not till you're
past the perimeter.</i>

32:10.770 --> 32:14.710
<i>As long as my ship can
keep up with you, I'll stay.</i>

32:14.710 --> 32:16.740
Approaching Side 6's
airspace borderline.

32:16.740 --> 32:19.420
Full combat speed!
Are our mobile suits ready?

32:19.420 --> 32:22.410
Gundam! 108! 109!
We're going to full combat speed.

32:23.290 --> 32:25.070
<i>Cameron!</i>

32:25.070 --> 32:26.360
Lieutenant...

32:26.360 --> 32:30.010
<i>Pull back! We're probably
going to have to fight.</i>

32:30.010 --> 32:33.630
<i>Cameron, thank you.
You've proven yourself to me.</i>

32:34.270 --> 32:38.630
<i>But... Thank you,
Cameron. Now go.</i>

32:38.630 --> 32:41.160
<i>Give my best to
your father and mother.</i>

32:41.880 --> 32:43.440
Mirai...

32:43.440 --> 32:45.270
I'm turning back!

32:46.980 --> 32:48.390
Please! Take us to the bridge!

33:08.070 --> 33:12.940
108! 109! Mega-particle cannons!
Open fire on the trailing Musai!

33:12.940 --> 33:14.460
I know it's playing dirty,
but they still can't fire.

33:26.590 --> 33:28.310
They got the Kramel?!

33:28.310 --> 33:32.510
Damned Trojan Horse! Firing
while we still can't isn't fair!

33:32.510 --> 33:34.070
To hell with this!
Fire! Fire!

33:37.100 --> 33:37.880
It's started <i>...</i>

33:37.880 --> 33:39.180
A TV Ship!

33:42.240 --> 33:42.990
Mirai...

33:48.450 --> 33:51.300
<i>This is not a drama,
but a real battle!</i>

33:51.300 --> 33:55.590
<i>Federal and Zeon ships,
fighting in a corner of space.</i>

33:56.080 --> 33:58.040
Never mind the White Basel

33:58.040 --> 34:00.510
Show me the Gundam!
Show me how well it's fighting!

34:00.510 --> 34:02.240
Yes, there we <i>go...</i>

34:02.240 --> 34:04.720
Dammit, Amuro!
What are you doing?!

34:04.720 --> 34:07.010
Concentrate fire
on that other Musai!

34:07.010 --> 34:09.310
Have Hayato's 109 cover Amuro!

34:11.430 --> 34:13.860
Damn, guess I'll just die
in this metal coffin.

34:13.860 --> 34:16.490
Hey, bridge! Aren't you
gonna launch the Core-Boosters?

34:18.200 --> 34:21.830
<i>I've gotten used to this.
I see that now.</i>

34:35.660 --> 34:37.380
Four!

34:38.660 --> 34:41.520
<i>As I keep telling you,
this is a real battle!</i>

34:41.520 --> 34:45.150
<i>A battle occurring right
outside of Side 6!</i>

34:45.150 --> 34:47.750
<i>Can the lone Federal ship, the White Base,
escape the encircling Zeon forces?</i>

34:47.750 --> 34:51.130
Have they been treating you
well at the Flanagan Institute?

34:51.130 --> 34:54.630
Yes. I'm their
star pupil, after all.

34:54.630 --> 34:57.930
I guess so. Take a good look.

34:57.930 --> 35:01.940
A real battle isn't thrilling,
like a TV show.

35:01.940 --> 35:04.270
This is what the
battlefield looks like.

35:04.270 --> 35:05.490
I know.

35:05.490 --> 35:07.750
<i>Watching this battle
occurring on our doorstep...</i>

35:07.750 --> 35:11.840
<i>...forces us to consider how we
can avoid being drawn into this war.</i>

35:11.840 --> 35:15.830
Yes, that's the way!
It's Amuro! It's the Gundam!

35:18.700 --> 35:21.490
The white mobile suit will win.

35:21.800 --> 35:24.430
They aren't showing the Gundam.

35:24.430 --> 35:29.430
I just know. That's why you
hang around with a girl like me.

35:31.110 --> 35:33.370
You're perceptive, Lalah.

35:35.450 --> 35:39.440
I hate it when you talk that way.
You sound too grown up.

35:39.440 --> 35:41.530
Do I? I'll try to avoid it.

35:49.160 --> 35:50.620
Seven!

36:01.210 --> 36:02.510
Hands off, pall

36:07.050 --> 36:08.600
Eight!

36:20.230 --> 36:21.230
Nine!

36:23.260 --> 36:27.790
Destroyed?!
Twelve Rick-Dome, destroyed?!

36:27.790 --> 36:29.800
They've been fighting
for less than 3 minutes!

36:29.800 --> 36:30.990
Yes, sir!

36:30.990 --> 36:35.860
One damaged warship
took out twelve Rick-Doms...

36:35.860 --> 36:37.930
They're not human!

36:37.930 --> 36:39.730
Gundam, closing in!

36:39.730 --> 36:42.500
Shoot it down!
Char is watching this!

36:46.090 --> 36:49.390
No energy left in my rifle, but
I have to try and finish them!

37:08.980 --> 37:10.570
Well, Captain?

37:10.570 --> 37:13.120
I said you were perceptive, Lalah.

37:15.450 --> 37:20.470
The Gundam pilot's Newtype
abilities have begun to awaken.

37:20.470 --> 37:22.840
At a level close to yours.

37:23.130 --> 37:25.500
Perhaps higher.

37:25.500 --> 37:26.920
Yes, sir.

37:27.130 --> 37:31.260
They won! They won!
It must have been the new module!

37:31.260 --> 37:32.850
Take that, you damn Zeon!

37:32.850 --> 37:35.890
The Gundam still has
some life left in it!

37:37.870 --> 37:40.760
The Federal Forces are going to win!

37:46.350 --> 37:48.600
Hooray for the Earth Federation!

37:48.600 --> 37:50.840
Hooray!

38:05.000 --> 38:08.190
Enough... Take us home.

38:11.300 --> 38:15.600
<i>Come through this alive, Mirai...</i>

38:19.610 --> 38:21.070
It's highly probable that...

38:21.070 --> 38:24.480
...the Earth Federation will attempt
a blitz on Solomon.

38:24.480 --> 38:26.780
But don't worry, Dozle.

38:26.780 --> 38:29.950
I assume you'll be committing
your Newtypes to the battle.

38:30.360 --> 38:33.780
<i>Of course, although we have
a few more tests to run.</i>

38:33.780 --> 38:36.930
<i>We'll send what reinforcements
we can from Granada.</i>

38:36.930 --> 38:38.820
<i>Use A Baoa Qu!</i>

38:38.820 --> 38:43.020
<i>Transfer troops from A Baoa Qu
while there's still time!</i>

38:43.020 --> 38:47.090
You'll have them. We're
preparing to send them to you.

38:47.090 --> 38:49.750
We've also sent you
the Big-Zam as well.

38:49.750 --> 38:52.430
That single machine has the strength
of two or three divisions.

38:52.980 --> 38:54.870
<i>Battles are won
by numbers, big brother!</i>

38:54.870 --> 38:58.120
<i>You should have a way to win
before you get so arrogant!</i>

38:58.120 --> 38:59.640
I know!

38:59.640 --> 39:02.680
Our father, Degwin, was stubborn,
which slowed us down...

39:02.680 --> 39:04.970
...but the plan is now set.

39:05.890 --> 39:07.990
I'm also sending out reinforcements.

39:07.990 --> 39:11.390
But there's now the risk that our
conversations will be overheard.

39:11.390 --> 39:15.770
From now on, simply follow
your written orders, Dozle.

39:15.770 --> 39:16.620
And you, Kycilia.

39:16.620 --> 39:19.120
<i>Yes, brother. And you.</i>

39:19.120 --> 39:22.900
Dozle, hold that base
and Zeon will be victorious.

39:38.260 --> 39:42.360
Well, the Solar-Ray can
always be used in other ways.

39:42.360 --> 39:43.560
It won't be wasted.

39:48.230 --> 39:52.300
I'm just a puppet. You know
Lord Gihren controls the Assembly.

39:52.300 --> 39:55.430
Suppose an offer for
peace suddenly appeared.

39:55.430 --> 39:57.770
Would that buy you some time?

39:57.770 --> 40:01.400
Perhaps. I may be able
to sway the Assembly, but...

40:01.400 --> 40:03.110
Damn you, Gihren.

40:03.110 --> 40:06.210
Didn't your brother's
death affect you at all?

40:06.210 --> 40:08.140
You aren't normal.

40:08.710 --> 40:13.420
As long as Solomon and Granada exist,
I'll try to open a route for us.

40:16.970 --> 40:20.310
- Wow! A wrecked colony!
- Even its mirrors are broken!

40:20.310 --> 40:22.660
108 and 109 will
remain outside the colony.

40:22.660 --> 40:24.100
The Gundam will
investigate the inside.

40:24.100 --> 40:25.330
Aye, sir!

40:25.330 --> 40:27.630
How long till we rendezvous
with Wakkein's fleet?

40:27.630 --> 40:28.900
Three hours, sir.

40:30.180 --> 40:32.360
<i>Texas colony.</i>

40:32.360 --> 40:36.570
<i>Originally built to raise
farm animals and for sightseeing.</i>

40:36.570 --> 40:41.550
<i>Abandoned due to the war,
its mirrors no longer function.</i> ,,

40:41.550 --> 40:45.680
<i>...and it has now become a
barely inhabitable desert.</i>

40:51.330 --> 40:57.430
She has a 70% target accuracy rate.
Ensign Lalah is truly amazing.

40:57.430 --> 40:59.020
I'm returning to the Zanzibar.

40:59.020 --> 41:01.930
I still need
to fine-tune my Gelgoog.

41:01.930 --> 41:04.800
I need more time to
calibrate the psy-commu system.

41:04.800 --> 41:07.340
Although Lady Kycilia is
urging us to finish quickly...

41:07.340 --> 41:10.670
<i>...if</i> the Elmeth isn't ready
in time, it won't be much use.

41:10.670 --> 41:11.520
What was that?

41:12.490 --> 41:13.870
What's wrong?

41:17.190 --> 41:19.990
I felt you touching
my mind, Captain.

41:21.790 --> 41:23.910
Could you please
not joke like that?

41:38.750 --> 41:39.870
You're sure?

41:39.870 --> 41:43.670
Yes, sir. We spotted
two unidentified fighters.

41:43.670 --> 41:44.810
Lalah!

41:45.420 --> 41:47.680
You should get back to the
Zanzibar, too, Dr. Flanagan.

41:48.320 --> 41:52.750
Lalah, was that feeling you had
before due to the enemy drawing near?

41:52.750 --> 41:57.230
It felt gentle, like
when I sense you, Captain.

41:57.230 --> 41:59.260
I don't think it was.

41:59.260 --> 42:04.970
But, does this mean
you'll still fight for <i>us...</i>

42:04.970 --> 42:07.800
...once you're able to read
your enemy's intentions?

42:07.800 --> 42:11.900
I want to protect you, Captain.

42:11.900 --> 42:15.700
But all I love about
you are your abilities.

42:15.700 --> 42:17.780
I don't care.

42:17.780 --> 42:20.280
That's only because you're a man.

42:20.280 --> 42:24.910
That's why I keep
my integrity as a woman.

42:24.910 --> 42:26.890
I hope you won't
find it a nuisance.

42:28.390 --> 42:32.350
You're strong, Lalah.
That's what I like about you.

42:33.870 --> 42:35.390
Thank you, sir.

42:35.390 --> 42:36.590
Don't mention it.

42:37.770 --> 42:39.430
Well, Mulligan?

42:39.430 --> 42:42.900
It's one ship, but it seems to have
parked at the opposite bay block.

42:42.900 --> 42:45.230
Is my Gelgoog ready to sortie?

42:45.230 --> 42:46.170
But, sir!

42:46.170 --> 42:48.120
This recon will
double as a field test.

42:48.120 --> 42:49.610
Just be ready
to get out of here!

42:49.610 --> 42:50.620
Yes, sir!

43:01.790 --> 43:04.390
I knew it! There is
something going on in here!

43:06.400 --> 43:10.820
I know! I've memorized
the data on the Gelgoog!

43:11.310 --> 43:14.190
Won't you wear
a normal suit, sir?

43:14.190 --> 43:16.240
My policy is to assume
I'll come back alive...

43:16.240 --> 43:18.480
...even when I'm
piloting a mobile suit.

43:25.520 --> 43:27.740
The Zeon have laid mines!

43:42.970 --> 43:45.360
<i>We may encounter
enemy mobile suits.</i>

43:45.360 --> 43:47.760
<i>If we do, pull back to
a safe spot to watch.</i>

43:47.960 --> 43:49.270
Yes, sir.

44:01.890 --> 44:03.490
Did he get caught in the minefield?

44:08.230 --> 44:10.860
This whole block's a minefield!

44:10.860 --> 44:13.720
I'll have to fly to the
opposite bay block in one go.

44:19.510 --> 44:20.840
A red mobile suit!

44:27.310 --> 44:28.640
The Gundam!

45:05.120 --> 45:05.880
Char!

45:09.560 --> 45:13.080
This feeling I have...
Like the one I felt before...

45:16.300 --> 45:19.850
If I lead him into the nuclear minefield,
even the Gundam can't...I

45:28.040 --> 45:29.670
He's jumping into the minefield!

45:29.670 --> 45:31.130
Lalah, get down!

45:37.650 --> 45:39.080
Captain!

46:12.350 --> 46:13.700
Who are you?

46:16.660 --> 46:20.510
Who is it? Who do
I feel looking at me?

46:21.930 --> 46:23.920
<i>Hurry. Get back
to the Zanzibar!</i>

46:23.920 --> 46:25.590
Yes, Captain.

46:26.170 --> 46:28.590
<i>The airflow's slowed,
but it's still dangerous.</i>

46:28.590 --> 46:29.630
<i>I'll be back shortly.</i>

46:40.210 --> 46:41.810
<i>He saw an explosion?</i>

46:41.810 --> 46:45.480
Yeah. Lieutenant Sleggar saw
it on the colony's hull.

46:50.420 --> 46:52.210
Nothing else unusual
since that explosion.

46:52.210 --> 46:54.980
Take us in! There might
be more reinforcements!

46:54.980 --> 46:55.950
All ahead, slow.

47:03.900 --> 47:06.630
No good... Where's Char?

47:11.580 --> 47:13.340
Char?

47:13.650 --> 47:15.300
I doubt it.

47:15.780 --> 47:17.170
Come on, move!

47:27.730 --> 47:32.080
I doubt that dummy explosion
will fool that pilot.

47:36.100 --> 47:39.830
Hayato! I saw an
explosion in C-block! See it?

47:40.000 --> 47:43.500
No, I was concentrating
on the opposite bay block!

47:47.210 --> 47:51.750
Kai! Hayato! Do you read?
Check out the other bay block.

47:51.750 --> 47:54.570
Remember, there may be
an enemy ship in there.

47:54.570 --> 47:56.580
We'll send out separate
parties to look for the Gundam!

47:56.580 --> 48:00.970
Fraw! Have Kimura, Rohl, Omur,
Sayla, and Job stand by in buggies!

48:00.970 --> 48:03.020
Aye, sir. Calling hatch #3.

48:08.630 --> 48:12.160
Main cannon! Mega-particle cannons!
Target the opposite bay block!

48:12.160 --> 48:14.540
We don't know when
the enemy might appear!

48:14.540 --> 48:16.730
Mirai, keep the
engines at critical.

48:16.730 --> 48:17.660
Aye, sir.

48:22.110 --> 48:25.400
Fraw, patch the buggies'
com. circuits into my station.

48:25.400 --> 48:26.640
Aye, sir.

48:26.640 --> 48:28.000
Go ahead.

48:28.620 --> 48:30.680
Continue monitoring messages
from Kai and Hayato.

48:30.680 --> 48:31.380
Aye, sir.

49:06.490 --> 49:07.750
Artesia!

49:08.590 --> 49:09.420
Big brother...

49:14.100 --> 49:17.470
Didn't I tell you to leave
the Forces? Now you're an officer.

49:17.470 --> 49:21.600
You're the one who
left me to avenge Father.

49:21.600 --> 49:25.150
You became a soldier...
Turned against the Earth Federation.

49:25.150 --> 49:26.640
Aren't you the one
who's made the mistake?!

49:27.810 --> 49:31.040
<i>Who's she talking to?
That voice.</i>

49:31.520 --> 49:34.240
Jimba Ral, when he raised <i>us...</i>

49:34.240 --> 49:38.340
...told us how Sovereign Degwin
Zabi assassinated our father.

49:38.340 --> 49:41.620
I know.
He always talked about it.

49:42.260 --> 49:47.390
<i>It was Degwin who arranged for the
heart attack that killed Father.</i>

49:47.390 --> 49:51.620
<i>Degwin only named the Principality
after him when he took control...</i>

49:51.620 --> 49:55.300
<i>...to avoid anyone
suspecting him of killing him.</i>

49:55.770 --> 50:02.310
<i>Degwin twisted Father's argument
for Spacenoid independence...</i>

50:02.310 --> 50:04.810
<i>...into the idea that
they were a Newtype elite.</i>

50:06.140 --> 50:12.350
And that, as the spaceborn elite,
they didn't have to obey Earth.

50:12.520 --> 50:14.110
But, in this war...

50:14.310 --> 50:18.300
No, even before it began,
people began changing out here.

50:18.300 --> 50:21.450
Some people understand that,
and some people don't.

50:21.690 --> 50:24.560
That's why Oldtypes will be destroyed.

50:24.560 --> 50:28.750
But aren't Oldtypes the soil
from which Newtypes grow?

50:28.970 --> 50:31.630
Not everything that's
old is necessarily bad!

50:31.630 --> 50:36.180
I realize that! But, Artesia...

50:36.180 --> 50:38.180
I don't like how Newtypes
being taken in by the system...

50:38.180 --> 50:40.760
...are being made to be my enemies!

50:40.760 --> 50:44.340
They're getting in the way
of my killing the Zabi family!

50:44.340 --> 50:45.810
Amuro would understand...

50:46.160 --> 50:49.590
Amuro? The Gundam pilot?

50:49.590 --> 50:50.880
Yes.

50:51.830 --> 50:54.860
<i>What is this?
What are they talking about?</i>

50:55.470 --> 50:58.530
A pilot can't
change the whole system!

50:58.530 --> 51:02.570
His Newtype abilities are
just being used for war!

51:03.410 --> 51:06.470
Big brother!
What are you trying to do?!

51:06.470 --> 51:07.780
I'm going to avenge our father!

51:07.780 --> 51:09.310
You're lying!

51:09.310 --> 51:12.080
I know you're trying to do this
on your own, but...

51:12.080 --> 51:15.130
...you can't create some self-centered world
ruled over by Newtypes!

51:15.720 --> 51:17.880
I'm not nearly that conceited!

51:17.880 --> 51:22.420
I just want to let
Newtypes live <i>as</i> Newtypes!

51:24.700 --> 51:27.420
Artesia, leave the Trojan Horse.

51:27.420 --> 51:29.720
There's enough gold left to
let you go back to Earth.

51:29.720 --> 51:30.850
Big brother!

51:30.850 --> 51:33.830
Do you understand
why I wear this mask?

51:33.830 --> 51:36.460
I'm not the Casval
you once knew!

51:36.460 --> 51:39.940
I am Char Aznable!
A man who has abandoned his past!

51:39.940 --> 51:41.210
Big brother, I...

51:43.380 --> 51:45.860
Big brother! Casval!

51:48.150 --> 51:50.440
Casval!

51:50.440 --> 51:52.870
Big brother!

52:03.940 --> 52:06.190
What's wrong, Bright?
Is it Amuro?

52:06.190 --> 52:09.130
No, it's... It's nothing.

52:09.720 --> 52:11.460
The static's terrible.

52:11.460 --> 52:12.700
Really?

52:12.700 --> 52:16.040
Y- Yeah...
I'm worried about Amuro.

52:16.040 --> 52:16.940
So am I.

52:16.940 --> 52:18.060
The Gundam's been found!

52:21.050 --> 52:22.370
Captain!

52:22.370 --> 52:23.740
The enemy ship
is the Trojan Horse!

52:23.740 --> 52:25.750
The Gelgoog's on board
along with the Elmeth.

52:25.750 --> 52:26.480
And Lalah?

52:26.480 --> 52:27.620
Yes, sir.

52:27.620 --> 52:30.590
They won't try anything until
they've recovered the Gundam.

52:30.590 --> 52:31.330
Get us out of here!

52:33.900 --> 52:35.530
Right! Mirai, launch!

52:35.530 --> 52:37.190
Exit through the bay the
Zanzibar was using!

52:37.190 --> 52:38.540
We may have to
fight a running battle!

52:47.250 --> 52:48.390
A mine?

52:55.050 --> 53:00.830
All I know is that the letter in
the trunk was addressed to you.

53:00.830 --> 53:05.450
Kai's keeping his mouth shut.
You know what this is about, right?

53:06.530 --> 53:07.930
<i>I do.</i>

53:07.930 --> 53:11.830
I could question you,
but won't you tell me yourself?

53:11.830 --> 53:14.730
What's in the trunk
and who wrote this letter?

53:14.730 --> 53:18.930
I think there's probably
gold in the trunk.

53:18.930 --> 53:20.600
You think so?

53:20.600 --> 53:21.400
Yes, I do.

53:21.400 --> 53:22.170
And the author of this letter?

53:22.710 --> 53:26.130
Char Aznable. The Red Comet.

53:29.220 --> 53:31.280
That's...

53:32.930 --> 53:33.720
Impossible!

53:36.160 --> 53:39.960
<i>“I beg that you promise to
do what I told you to."</i>

53:40.300 --> 53:45.420
<i>"To his gentle sister,
Artesia Som Deikun... "</i>

53:45.420 --> 53:49.430
<i>“...Casval Rem Deikun sends his love. "</i>

53:54.580 --> 53:56.170
Big brother...

53:59.050 --> 54:01.570
Casval. <i>..</i>

54:11.500 --> 54:13.850
Now don't move from here!

54:13.850 --> 54:15.160
Yes, sir.

54:15.160 --> 54:18.030
What did Kycilia
say from Granada?

54:18.030 --> 54:20.520
She's sending reinforcements.

54:21.170 --> 54:24.360
And what about Gihren's Solar-Ray?

54:24.360 --> 54:27.800
It looks like Sovereign Degwin's
having second thoughts about it.

54:27.800 --> 54:30.360
Does Father want Solomon to fall?!

54:41.000 --> 54:42.710
<i>Our fleet is currently
standing by at...</i>

54:42.710 --> 54:45.850
<i>...the third battle
line opposite Solomon.</i>

54:45.850 --> 54:48.930
<i>Beyond this point there is
no more wreckage from Side 4.</i>

54:48.930 --> 54:50.890
<i>Even if we are
attacked from Solomon,</i> ,,

54:50.890 --> 54:53.770
<i>...we will not open fire until
we reach the second battle line.</i>

54:53.770 --> 54:56.390
<i>The fleet will assume
a line abreast formation.</i>

54:59.240 --> 55:01.810
Okay, White Base.

55:01.810 --> 55:05.940
Show me how those amateurs
who came to Luna !I have grown.

55:20.330 --> 55:22.790
It's a light barrage! Don't fall
back! Just five more minutes!

55:27.140 --> 55:30.730
Not yet! We can't die yet!
Not till we've fired our missiles!

55:42.270 --> 55:43.950
La Coque! Take the conn!

55:43.950 --> 55:44.810
Yes, sir!

55:44.810 --> 55:46.560
I'll be right back!

55:50.230 --> 55:54.200
Expect the worst! Get the
women to the escape capsule!

55:57.700 --> 55:58.850
Hurry.

55:58.850 --> 56:01.230
Is the battle going that badly?

56:01.230 --> 56:01.960
I said hurry!

56:01.960 --> 56:03.400
Y- Yes, sir!

56:03.400 --> 56:09.010
Solomon won't fall. But we should
be prepared, just in case!

56:09.010 --> 56:14.270
Now that I have her...
For Mineva's sake, I can't lose.

56:15.790 --> 56:17.800
Your voice is so loud.

56:20.930 --> 56:21.930
Move it!

56:21.930 --> 56:22.890
Incoming!

56:30.140 --> 56:34.360
Dammit! Not here!
I won't die alone!

56:37.210 --> 56:40.230
<i>Who will live? Who will die?</i>

56:40.780 --> 56:43.790
<i>That will not be known
until the Dame's end.</i>

56:44.220 --> 56:49.080
<i>All that can be certain is
that each beautiful sparkle...</i>

56:49.080 --> 56:58.120
<i>...shows one or hundreds of people
being blown to stardust.</i>

57:07.640 --> 57:08.630
Are the mirrors set?

57:08.630 --> 57:10.900
Sir! Just four more minutes, sir!

57:10.900 --> 57:13.570
Hm... Solomon's
going to notice us soon.

57:14.180 --> 57:18.840
What?! That's impossible!
Hidden in the wreckage of Side 1?!

57:18.840 --> 57:19.810
What?

57:19.810 --> 57:21.620
Tianem's main fleet!

57:27.990 --> 57:32.090
Send the Gwaran and some Musais
towards the main enemy fleet!

57:33.030 --> 57:35.880
Shall we ask the 7th
Division for support?

57:35.880 --> 57:37.860
Ask Kycilia?

57:39.140 --> 57:43.440
If I do that, I'll become the
laughingstock of our nation!

57:49.250 --> 57:52.900
Solar-System! Target Solomon's
right wing. The space gate!

58:05.120 --> 58:06.450
10 seconds to alignment.

58:06.450 --> 58:07.390
Activate mirrors!

58:07.390 --> 58:08.620
Counterattack units closing!
All ships, be prepared!

58:08.860 --> 58:10.960
Forget it!
Hurry up and focus!

58:14.070 --> 58:16.710
Three, two, entering focus!

58:33.020 --> 58:36.750
Solomon...!
It's burning! What's...?!

58:36.750 --> 58:39.360
Is that the power of the
Federal Forces' new weapon?!

58:43.990 --> 58:44.690
What's happening?!

58:44.690 --> 58:47.290
Space gate #6 is gone!
They have a new weapon!

58:47.290 --> 58:48.390
What is it?!

58:48.390 --> 58:51.690
Nothing on the radar!
No sign of energy particles!

58:52.500 --> 58:55.070
Is it a laser?! Where's the source?!

58:55.070 --> 58:56.790
The enemy's main fleet!

58:56.790 --> 58:58.470
Didn't we send the
Gwaran Fleet that way?!

58:58.470 --> 58:59.200
Yes, sir!

58:59.200 --> 59:00.610
109, recovered!

59:00.610 --> 59:02.610
Damage level: Bl
Pilot is wounded!

59:02.610 --> 59:06.510
Our battle strength is down
11% since 109 pulled back!

59:07.260 --> 59:09.830
- Oh, it's nothing serious.
- Really?

59:09.830 --> 59:13.420
Okay, just give Hayato another
unit of blood. Don't forget.

59:13.420 --> 59:14.850
Right.

59:18.000 --> 59:19.560
They're coming! The Dom...

59:19.560 --> 59:20.860
Hayato...

59:24.180 --> 59:25.000
Fraw Bow...

59:25.000 --> 59:29.410
Just be quiet. You fought well.
Get some rest, now.

59:29.410 --> 59:30.410
The others...?

59:30.410 --> 59:32.480
They're fine. Still in the fight.

59:32.480 --> 59:33.910
Oh...

59:34.590 --> 59:38.410
I hate <i>this...</i>
Why did it have to be me?

59:38.410 --> 59:43.050
I'm not as good as Kai or
even Sayla. I'm pathetic!

59:43.050 --> 59:46.350
What are you saying, Hayato?
You did a great job.

59:46.350 --> 59:50.320
Stop it! I don't want you
to make me feel better!

59:50.320 --> 59:54.060
All I've wanted, ever since
I came onto the White Base...

59:54.060 --> 59:59.610
<i>...was</i> to somehow be
better than Amuro. And now...

59:59.610 --> 01:00:00.990
I'm pathetic!

01:00:00.990 --> 01:00:02.570
Hayato...

01:00:04.480 --> 01:00:09.580
Amuro's different.
He's not like the rest of us.

01:00:16.090 --> 01:00:19.300
What? Solomon's
requesting reinforcements?

01:00:19.300 --> 01:00:23.650
Aye, sir! I can't make out
the details from the coded signal...

01:00:23.650 --> 01:00:27.430
...but Lady Kycilia is
ordering troops to Solomon.

01:00:28.010 --> 01:00:29.730
I doubt we'll make it, but...

01:00:29.730 --> 01:00:31.090
Yes, sir.

01:00:31.440 --> 01:00:33.930
Maximum combat speed!
Target: Solomon!

01:00:39.890 --> 01:00:41.400
Is Zenna here?

01:00:41.400 --> 01:00:43.740
Dear, aren't you coming?

01:00:43.740 --> 01:00:46.820
Don't be ridiculous!
Solomon isn't going to fall!

01:00:46.820 --> 01:00:47.550
But...

01:00:47.550 --> 01:00:51.220
No, just get out of here
and get to my sister at Granada.

01:00:51.220 --> 01:00:52.990
But you won't come?

01:00:52.990 --> 01:00:55.660
It's okay. Don't worry.

01:00:55.660 --> 01:00:58.880
Bring Mineva up to be a strong girl.

01:00:58.880 --> 01:01:00.790
Dear...

01:01:00.790 --> 01:01:03.380
I'm a soldier.

01:01:03.380 --> 01:01:06.740
A soldier who will build
the Zabi family's legacy.

01:01:07.680 --> 01:01:09.510
I won't die.

01:01:09.980 --> 01:01:12.930
Go, Zenna! Take Mineva and go!

01:01:17.020 --> 01:01:20.360
Great! I really
pulled a boner just now.

01:01:20.360 --> 01:01:22.750
Sleggar in 005
is returning to the ship!

01:01:22.750 --> 01:01:24.290
He's been hit
in the portside engine!

01:01:24.290 --> 01:01:25.360
Hatch #4, prep to receive!

01:01:25.560 --> 01:01:27.990
Sleggar, do you read?
Please respond!

01:01:27.990 --> 01:01:31.360
<i>I read you. I'll bring
her in on deck #3.</i>

01:01:32.540 --> 01:01:34.120
What is it, Ensign?

01:01:34.120 --> 01:01:36.250
N- Nothing, sir.

01:01:37.010 --> 01:01:40.490
Our starboard missile barrage
is too light! Pour it on!

01:01:40.490 --> 01:01:44.570
Fraw Bow! Get Chief Vammas
up here from the sub-bridge!

01:01:44.920 --> 01:01:46.440
<i>Ensign Mirai.</i>

01:01:51.060 --> 01:01:53.300
<i>I know private conversations are
forbidden during battle, but...</i>

01:01:54.030 --> 01:01:55.990
<i>You're being very distant, Mirai.</i>

01:01:55.990 --> 01:01:59.690
<i>I could be the one who
could care for you, but.</i> ,,

01:02:00.700 --> 01:02:01.520
<i>Bright...</i>

01:02:02.300 --> 01:02:07.330
<i>I know how you feel about him,
but I'm prepared to wait.</i>

01:02:07.330 --> 01:02:08.160
Yes, sir?

01:02:08.160 --> 01:02:09.990
Ensign Mirai's
feeling a little sick.

01:02:09.990 --> 01:02:11.930
Will you relieve
her for a while?

01:02:11.930 --> 01:02:13.570
Aye, sir! I've got it.

01:02:14.450 --> 01:02:15.230
<i>Bright...</i>

01:02:15.230 --> 01:02:18.400
A- A guns, incoming to port!
Do you see it?!

01:02:18.400 --> 01:02:21.380
Hurry up! Let's try
to do this in 10 minutes!

01:02:21.380 --> 01:02:22.710
- Howard!
- Yeah?

01:02:22.710 --> 01:02:24.480
Where's Lieutenant Sleggar?

01:02:24.480 --> 01:02:26.550
He was headed for
the starboard ready room.

01:02:26.550 --> 01:02:28.410
I see. Thanks.

01:02:39.400 --> 01:02:42.230
Lieutenant... You aren't hurt.

01:02:43.210 --> 01:02:46.900
What are you doing here, Ensign?

01:02:59.120 --> 01:03:00.830
Thank God...

01:03:01.560 --> 01:03:05.020
Let's stop it right here,
Ensign. It won't work.

01:03:05.020 --> 01:03:08.080
<i>Lieutenant Sleggar!
Prepare to launch!</i>

01:03:08.080 --> 01:03:09.520
Gotta go.

01:03:10.140 --> 01:03:11.670
See you.

01:03:11.670 --> 01:03:12.430
Lieutenant...

01:03:18.610 --> 01:03:20.310
Come back to me safely.

01:03:24.820 --> 01:03:26.760
Ensign Mirai...

01:03:26.760 --> 01:03:29.400
People go through a lot of
things when they're young.

01:03:29.400 --> 01:03:33.240
Maybe you shouldn't take these
feelings you have seriously.

01:03:33.240 --> 01:03:35.050
What do you mean?

01:03:35.050 --> 01:03:38.610
Hm? Oh, never mind.

01:03:38.610 --> 01:03:39.720
Lieutenant!

01:03:43.460 --> 01:03:47.340
I'm not the son of man who could
accept what you have to give.

01:03:48.410 --> 01:03:49.340
Sleggar...

01:03:49.540 --> 01:03:54.330
You're... A star that
shines too bright for me.

01:03:54.330 --> 01:03:55.800
We live in different worlds.

01:03:55.800 --> 01:03:56.940
But...

01:03:57.850 --> 01:04:01.590
This isn't much.
It's a keepsake from my mom.

01:04:01.590 --> 01:04:03.770
I wouldn't want it
to get lost in space.

01:04:03.770 --> 01:04:04.600
Would you take care of it for me?

01:04:11.460 --> 01:04:12.810
Thanks.

01:04:26.340 --> 01:04:28.380
Take care of that ring, Ensign!

01:04:42.790 --> 01:04:44.350
Lieutenant...

01:04:45.100 --> 01:04:49.980
<i>Granada, the base for Kycilia
Zabi's mobile space forces.</i>

01:04:51.040 --> 01:04:53.670
<i>The reinforcements
were launching...</i>

01:04:53.670 --> 01:04:55.700
<i>...though it was clear
they were far too late.</i>

01:05:14.860 --> 01:05:15.840
Th- The beams!

01:05:32.040 --> 01:05:32.820
What them?!

01:05:45.160 --> 01:05:47.480
Our remaining ships are
charging the main enemy fleet!

01:05:47.480 --> 01:05:48.350
Excellent!

01:05:48.350 --> 01:05:49.650
What's the Big-Zam's target?

01:05:49.650 --> 01:05:51.420
Aim for the command ships
hanging to the rear!

01:05:51.420 --> 01:05:52.630
Ignore the cannon fodder!

01:05:52.630 --> 01:05:53.720
Salamis ahead!

01:05:53.720 --> 01:05:56.170
Forget it!
Fire the forward beam cannon!

01:06:02.240 --> 01:06:06.040
A huge, two-legged mobile suit!
The beams are bouncing off it!

01:06:06.040 --> 01:06:06.850
The 005!

01:06:08.450 --> 01:06:10.900
Not bad, Lieutenant Sleggar.

01:06:11.110 --> 01:06:13.870
Have the Big-Zam
attack the main fleet!

01:06:13.870 --> 01:06:17.210
But, before we do, launch the
flare to signal the evacuation!

01:06:17.210 --> 01:06:18.820
Aye! But, sir...!

01:06:19.360 --> 01:06:22.150
Our forces are too scattered.

01:06:22.150 --> 01:06:24.690
I don't like it, but we
have to abandon Solomon.

01:06:24.690 --> 01:06:29.500
Transfer control over to my
station and save yourselves!

01:06:29.690 --> 01:06:31.390
<i>But, Admiral...!</i>

01:06:31.390 --> 01:06:32.810
Don't throw your lives away!

01:06:32.810 --> 01:06:34.430
We still have Doms and Zakus.

01:06:34.430 --> 01:06:36.830
They can tow you
out of the battle zone!

01:06:36.830 --> 01:06:38.060
Yes, sir.

01:06:38.060 --> 01:06:42.340
Right! Fire the signal flare!
I'm taking control of the Big-Zam!

01:06:50.120 --> 01:06:53.350
To think Solomon
would fall so easily...

01:07:01.270 --> 01:07:02.070
The Gundam!

01:07:04.300 --> 01:07:07.220
That's hard to take on.

01:07:14.050 --> 01:07:15.440
Don't underestimate the Big-Zam!

01:07:15.440 --> 01:07:18.980
It's impervious to long-range
beam bombardment!

01:07:18.980 --> 01:07:22.260
I'll take as many of you as
I can down to hell with me!

01:07:35.690 --> 01:07:37.360
It's unstoppable!

01:07:38.600 --> 01:07:42.030
Do you see?! When we
mass-produce the Big-Zam...

01:07:42.030 --> 01:07:44.070
...you Feddies will be
dead before you realize it!

01:07:51.020 --> 01:07:54.340
Man, we can't just sit
here and let him do that!

01:07:54.340 --> 01:07:57.240
Hey, Gundam-boy!
Let's get that thing!

01:07:58.840 --> 01:08:02.300
You mean we have to attack it directly
because of that beam barrier?

01:08:02.480 --> 01:08:04.680
It sucks, but this is war, after all.

01:08:17.280 --> 01:08:19.190
From below?!
Air defenses, fire!

01:08:23.610 --> 01:08:25.200
You won't beat me!

01:08:29.620 --> 01:08:30.580
Damn you!

01:08:31.660 --> 01:08:32.750
The Gundam!

01:08:42.530 --> 01:08:44.390
<i>Why, you...I</i>

01:08:47.570 --> 01:08:50.890
The Big-Zam won't be beaten...

01:08:51.310 --> 01:08:53.680
<i>...by</i> just one mobile suit!

01:08:55.270 --> 01:08:56.980
I won't be beaten!

01:08:56.980 --> 01:09:00.360
One mobile suit cannot
defeat the glory of Zeon!

01:09:00.990 --> 01:09:03.730
As long as I live,
you won't beat Zeon!

01:09:04.520 --> 01:09:07.990
Who is that? Wha...?!

01:09:11.700 --> 01:09:12.830
<i>What is it...?!</i>

01:09:42.290 --> 01:09:45.480
Solomon has fallen?

01:09:45.480 --> 01:09:46.880
Yes, sir.

01:09:51.440 --> 01:09:56.960
We should be grateful to have at
least saved Lady Zenna and Mineva.

01:09:57.440 --> 01:09:59.940
If only it had
held a little longer...

01:09:59.940 --> 01:10:04.190
Yes, sir. We'd better reinforce
A Baoa Qu and Granada.

01:10:04.190 --> 01:10:06.510
Yes, quite right.

01:10:22.530 --> 01:10:24.650
Everyone has
to die eventually.

01:10:41.690 --> 01:10:44.650
<i>The Principality of Zeon
consists of...</i>

01:10:44.650 --> 01:10:46.920
<i>...approximately 40
closed-cylinder colonies.</i>

01:10:48.060 --> 01:10:51.660
<i>Its population numbers 150 million...</i>

01:10:51.660 --> 01:10:56.600
<i>...and it is the Side
least damaged by the war.</i>

01:10:57.140 --> 01:11:00.130
We can't just sit on
our hands simply because...

01:11:00.130 --> 01:11:02.170
...our reinforcements
didn't make it to Solomon.

01:11:02.170 --> 01:11:05.900
Kycilia's Newtype Corps
is already...

01:11:05.900 --> 01:11:10.650
...planning to attack Solomon
as a test.

01:11:11.150 --> 01:11:14.110
You speak lightly
of the Newtype Corps.

01:11:15.520 --> 01:11:17.770
They're a convenience.

01:11:17.770 --> 01:11:20.350
Father, you talk of how...

01:11:20.350 --> 01:11:24.120
...the Principality was vital to the
realization of Zeon's ideas.

01:11:24.120 --> 01:11:26.260
This is the same.

01:11:26.260 --> 01:11:28.190
No, it isn't!

01:11:28.190 --> 01:11:30.760
The Earth Federation
recognized the Principality of Zeon...

01:11:30.760 --> 01:11:33.800
<i>...as</i> the first autonomous
Spacenoid nation!

01:11:33.800 --> 01:11:37.760
Deikun's methods could only effect
changes at the civilian level.

01:11:38.610 --> 01:11:42.480
The term “Newtype Corps" will
increase our peoples' morale.

01:11:42.650 --> 01:11:45.370
Then your decreasing it
in your displacing <i>of...</i>

01:11:45.370 --> 01:11:49.210
...millions of citizens
<i>so</i> you can use your Solar-Ray...

01:11:49.210 --> 01:11:52.110
...shows me that you're
an incompetent soldier!

01:11:52.110 --> 01:11:55.950
You dare say that to me?
Look at this!

01:11:56.790 --> 01:11:58.160
I've had enough
of your strategies!

01:12:01.100 --> 01:12:07.040
Moon and A Baoa Qu are the
Principality's last line of defense.

01:12:07.040 --> 01:12:11.840
Against them, the Federal
Forces can take three routes.

01:12:12.640 --> 01:12:15.870
If they break through here,
the Principality will be left naked.

01:12:15.870 --> 01:12:18.840
Before that happens,
we'll fire the Solar-Ray...

01:12:18.840 --> 01:12:21.040
...from inside Zeon airspace
and destroy the Federation fleet.

01:12:21.040 --> 01:12:22.740
This plan's strongest point
is that it allows us to...

01:12:22.740 --> 01:12:26.110
...modify an existing
closed-cylinder colony...

01:12:26.110 --> 01:12:27.650
...thereby saving us a great
deal of time and expense...

01:12:27.650 --> 01:12:30.770
...while guaranteeing
maximum results.

01:12:31.030 --> 01:12:33.100
This will authorize the project.

01:12:33.100 --> 01:12:35.980
Which you've already begun.

01:12:38.300 --> 01:12:43.230
With a 6 km wide laser, smashing
the Feddies should be no problem.

01:12:43.230 --> 01:12:44.830
Yes, sir.

01:12:45.180 --> 01:12:48.040
And when we win, then what?

01:12:48.040 --> 01:12:50.500
We finally solve the
overpopulation problem.

01:12:50.500 --> 01:12:54.450
To maintain balance, only the truly
worthy should be allowed to live.

01:12:54.450 --> 01:12:59.650
To ensure mankind's eternal existence,
the Earth system must be cleansed.

01:12:59.650 --> 01:13:03.850
Far easier to control a small
number of people, don't you think?

01:13:04.660 --> 01:13:08.420
Have you ever heard of
a man named Adolf Hitler?

01:13:08.420 --> 01:13:12.020
Hitler... Lived in
the Middle Ages, didn't he?

01:13:12.900 --> 01:13:17.360
He was a dictator. A man who couldn't
see where the world was headed.

01:13:18.580 --> 01:13:21.410
You're following in his footsteps.

01:13:23.280 --> 01:13:27.590
I participated in Zeon Deikun's
revolution as well!

01:13:27.590 --> 01:13:32.550
If the population continues to grow,
we will breed weakness.

01:13:32.550 --> 01:13:34.250
And weakness will lead to extinction.

01:13:34.830 --> 01:13:39.480
What has the Federation's
absolute democracy given us?

01:13:39.480 --> 01:13:42.190
An out-of-control
and corrupt bureaucracy.

01:13:42.190 --> 01:13:45.560
A growing mass of humanity
which gobbles up resources.

01:13:46.400 --> 01:13:52.410
Federation weakness
created this cannibalistic war.

01:13:52.410 --> 01:13:56.150
The human race has
exceeded its limits.

01:13:56.150 --> 01:13:58.570
I'll command from A Baoa Qu.

01:14:00.520 --> 01:14:03.080
I'll show you we can win.

01:14:03.080 --> 01:14:07.280
After that, we can await
the coming of the true Newtypes.

01:14:07.990 --> 01:14:11.290
See how the man who follows
in Hitler's footsteps can fight!

01:14:13.400 --> 01:14:16.490
He's full of rationalizations.

01:14:18.270 --> 01:14:21.690
God only knows
what Kycilia's planning...

01:14:22.440 --> 01:14:26.100
Hitler's followers ended
up trying to kill him!

01:14:32.080 --> 01:14:32.860
At ease!

01:14:33.080 --> 01:14:34.910
Welcome to The Confeito, sir!

01:14:34.910 --> 01:14:37.240
So, how does it feel
to be using Solomon?

01:14:37.240 --> 01:14:38.240
Wonderful.

01:14:39.320 --> 01:14:40.360
Newtypes?

01:14:41.190 --> 01:14:42.010
I'm not sure I understand.

01:14:42.010 --> 01:14:46.080
Propaganda, designed to mask
how exhausted they've become.

01:14:46.080 --> 01:14:49.320
But, General, what about the Gundam's
and White Base's victories?

01:14:49.320 --> 01:14:52.100
They probably doubt it.

01:14:52.700 --> 01:14:57.330
Newtypes are supposedly people
who can live without war.

01:14:58.130 --> 01:15:00.870
Not people with super-natural abilities.

01:15:01.880 --> 01:15:05.500
Have the orderly get me
some aspirin, would you?

01:15:05.500 --> 01:15:07.810
I wonder what's wrong? I don't
think I'm catching a cold, but...

01:15:08.550 --> 01:15:12.250
I hope not. Not this
close to the Operation Star-One.

01:15:15.260 --> 01:15:16.680
What is it?

01:15:37.110 --> 01:15:38.870
They don't see
anything out there?!

01:15:38.870 --> 01:15:41.040
We haven't finished laying
new power lines yet!

01:15:41.040 --> 01:15:42.640
How could we see it?!

01:15:42.640 --> 01:15:45.580
Hey, what happened?!
Area 38! Area 38!

01:15:45.580 --> 01:15:46.870
General...

01:16:25.300 --> 01:16:29.220
What's that? An explosion?
Marker, where's the enemy?!

01:16:29.740 --> 01:16:30.990
I don't see any!

01:16:30.990 --> 01:16:34.470
Minovsky particle density is
too high for me to track any.

01:16:34.470 --> 01:16:35.970
All hands, air raid watch!

01:16:35.970 --> 01:16:39.340
Launch the Core-Booster
and all mobile suits!

01:16:39.340 --> 01:16:40.930
What is this?

01:16:40.930 --> 01:16:43.670
Ensign, are you sick?

01:16:43.670 --> 01:16:45.140
No, just a strange feeling.

01:16:45.140 --> 01:16:48.620
Something's strange around
the Confeito.

01:16:48.620 --> 01:16:52.540
Strange... Like you were sensing
what was about to happen?

01:16:54.630 --> 01:16:56.540
<i>All hands! Go to emergency
combat alert level 1!</i>

01:17:00.570 --> 01:17:03.120
I thought we were
only on half-watch.

01:17:07.640 --> 01:17:08.430
Who's calling to me?

01:17:10.880 --> 01:17:11.930
What is this?

01:17:12.170 --> 01:17:14.890
Can't they cut us some slack?!

01:17:16.180 --> 01:17:17.240
Ensign Sayla!

01:17:17.240 --> 01:17:18.070
<i>Yes, sir?</i>

01:17:18.070 --> 01:17:21.460
I trust you, but leave your
personal feelings out of the battle.

01:17:21.460 --> 01:17:24.520
<i>I've been fighting
sincerely up till now, sir.</i>

01:17:24.520 --> 01:17:28.200
<i>Besides that, can you feel it?
This... oppressiveness?</i>

01:17:28.800 --> 01:17:30.820
No, nothing.

01:17:31.730 --> 01:17:33.950
Although Mirai was
just saying the same thing...

01:17:33.950 --> 01:17:35.790
<i>006, moving out!</i>

01:17:36.370 --> 01:17:38.230
Something wrong, Bright?

01:17:38.230 --> 01:17:42.170
Nothing. It's just that...
Something's bothering Sayla.

01:17:42.170 --> 01:17:43.880
Do you still feel it?

01:17:48.280 --> 01:17:52.510
<i>I don't blame him.
I know the Red Comet, after all.</i>

01:17:56.620 --> 01:17:58.910
How many ships has it taken out?

01:17:58.910 --> 01:18:03.420
<i>With the magnetic coating the Gundam's
a bit more maneuverable, but...</i>

01:18:12.820 --> 01:18:14.190
<i>They're calling me!</i>

01:18:51.010 --> 01:18:52.990
<i>What am I seeing?</i>

01:18:56.580 --> 01:18:57.910
Those lights there...

01:18:58.150 --> 01:19:01.570
They're from Lalah's attacks.
Incredible!

01:19:02.260 --> 01:19:03.380
<i>Captain...!</i>

01:19:03.380 --> 01:19:04.420
What is it?

01:19:04.420 --> 01:19:05.680
<i>My head hurts.</i>

01:19:05.680 --> 01:19:09.200
Hm... Level 9.4. Pretty rough.

01:19:09.200 --> 01:19:10.690
<i>I can still do it!</i>

01:19:10.690 --> 01:19:11.680
We're pulling out!

01:19:17.040 --> 01:19:18.100
It's gone.

01:19:18.840 --> 01:19:21.020
Sorry for the bother.

01:19:21.020 --> 01:19:22.430
That's all right.

01:19:25.280 --> 01:19:27.640
What do you want
at a time like this?

01:19:27.640 --> 01:19:30.370
I want to clear up
your misunderstandings.

01:19:30.370 --> 01:19:31.810
My misunderstandings?

01:19:31.810 --> 01:19:36.940
You're angry with me, right?
For hiding that I knew Char.

01:19:36.940 --> 01:19:38.120
Well, a bit.

01:19:38.120 --> 01:19:40.150
Char is my big brother.

01:19:40.150 --> 01:19:45.150
Brother?! Your brother?
But, then why...?

01:19:46.230 --> 01:19:49.050
Things are... complicated.

01:19:51.370 --> 01:19:53.970
You mean you're
leaving the ship?

01:19:55.210 --> 01:19:59.430
No... I don't really
think I could do that now.

01:19:59.430 --> 01:20:02.240
I've grown attached to the White Base.

01:20:02.780 --> 01:20:06.710
And when I think about my brother
trying to accomplish the impossible...

01:20:06.710 --> 01:20:07.980
<i>...I</i> wish I were dead!

01:20:07.980 --> 01:20:08.980
Sayla!

01:20:09.460 --> 01:20:11.440
He's become a monster!

01:20:11.760 --> 01:20:17.030
Saying he believes in Father's
ideals as he twists <i>them...</i>

01:20:17.030 --> 01:20:19.040
He's not the Casval I knew.

01:20:19.040 --> 01:20:20.420
A <i>monster...</i>

01:20:21.900 --> 01:20:23.620
ls Casval his real name?

01:20:23.620 --> 01:20:27.290
Yes. Casval... Deikun.

01:20:27.460 --> 01:20:28.470
What?

01:20:28.470 --> 01:20:31.160
My real name is Artesia Deikun.

01:20:31.160 --> 01:20:33.840
<i>Zeon's...!</i> You're <i>Zeon's...!</i>

01:20:33.840 --> 01:20:37.120
Yes! Yes, we're his children!

01:20:37.120 --> 01:20:41.880
But, that has nothing
to do with us now!

01:20:41.880 --> 01:20:45.240
Pursued by the Zabi family,
unable to live on Earth...

01:20:46.390 --> 01:20:49.720
Here. This is the
gold my brother gave me.

01:20:49.720 --> 01:20:52.260
I want to give it to
everyone on the White Base.

01:20:52.260 --> 01:20:54.420
Are you sure about this?

01:20:54.420 --> 01:20:56.590
I'd feel better this way.

01:20:56.590 --> 01:20:59.960
It may sound like
a selfish excuse, but...

01:21:03.980 --> 01:21:07.040
You've chosen a difficult path.

01:21:07.040 --> 01:21:08.500
I agree.

01:21:15.190 --> 01:21:17.650
Lady Kycilia!
Captain Char has arrived!

01:21:17.650 --> 01:21:19.420
Show him in.

01:21:20.760 --> 01:21:24.790
Capt. Char Aznable and
Ens. Lalah Sune, reporting!

01:21:24.790 --> 01:21:29.440
My forces are deploying along
the A Baoa Qu and Granada lines.

01:21:29.440 --> 01:21:32.860
Captain, I want you to take
command of my assault forces.

01:21:32.860 --> 01:21:33.900
<i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

01:21:33.900 --> 01:21:35.630
Ens. Lalah Sune.

01:21:35.630 --> 01:21:36.880
<i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

01:21:36.880 --> 01:21:40.760
Your test at
Solomon was a success.

01:21:41.080 --> 01:21:43.580
I'll be depending on your help.

01:21:43.580 --> 01:21:46.680
Yes, ma'am.
The military saved me.

01:21:46.680 --> 01:21:48.870
I'll do all I can to help.

01:21:49.520 --> 01:21:51.710
Captain, please
come to my room later on.

01:21:52.490 --> 01:21:53.650
Yes, ma'am!

01:21:55.460 --> 01:21:57.790
<i>Sovereign Degwin Zabi,
not waiting for...</i>

01:21:57.790 --> 01:22:01.600
<i>...Prime Minister Darcia's
peace plans to materialize...</i>

01:22:01.600 --> 01:22:07.100
<i>...decided to contact the Federal Forces himself.</i>

01:22:08.080 --> 01:22:13.740
<i>He was now desperate to
stop Gihren's plans. However...</i>

01:22:14.580 --> 01:22:19.620
You're old, Father.
And you're also far too late.

01:22:19.620 --> 01:22:20.680
Yes?

01:22:20.680 --> 01:22:23.110
<i>A message from technical
advisor Captain Asakura, sir.</i>

01:22:23.110 --> 01:22:25.240
Right. Put him through.

01:22:25.890 --> 01:22:28.660
<i>The Solar-Ray is now operational.</i>

01:22:28.660 --> 01:22:30.850
<i>It will achieve
maximum power in two hours.</i>

01:22:30.850 --> 01:22:33.220
<i>As the polarizing mirror
was created only for tests...</i>

01:22:33.220 --> 01:22:34.690
<i>...we'll only be
able to fire it once.</i>

01:22:34.690 --> 01:22:36.760
Are its capabilities
as we predicted?

01:22:36.760 --> 01:22:38.260
<i>Yes, sir. Definitely.</i>

01:22:43.310 --> 01:22:45.800
We'll soon be engaging
the left wing...

01:22:45.800 --> 01:22:47.270
...of the Federation's
advancing fleet.

01:22:48.350 --> 01:22:49.420
<i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

01:22:49.420 --> 01:22:52.980
As it appears they're ignoring
Granada and headed for A Baoa Qu...

01:22:52.980 --> 01:22:55.420
...my fleet can't
avoid engaging them.

01:22:55.420 --> 01:22:57.950
Gihren must see that we're
making an effort to fight.

01:22:57.950 --> 01:22:58.710
<i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

01:22:58.710 --> 01:23:00.290
What's wrong? Have a seat.

01:23:00.290 --> 01:23:02.090
Ah, yes, ma'am.

01:23:10.740 --> 01:23:14.880
As I thought. You do
resemble your father, actually.

01:23:14.880 --> 01:23:16.170
Yes.

01:23:16.580 --> 01:23:18.570
I never noticed.

01:23:18.570 --> 01:23:23.550
But, after all, Char Aznable is
<i>so</i> different from Casval Deikun.

01:23:24.920 --> 01:23:29.670
After I was cashiered by Admiral
Dozle and summoned by you...

01:23:29.670 --> 01:23:33.560
...I thought this day would come.

01:23:33.560 --> 01:23:38.710
I was afraid. Even now,
I can't keep my hands from shaking.

01:23:38.710 --> 01:23:40.660
I feel the same.

01:23:40.660 --> 01:23:43.620
Although, when I found out
who you really were, I laughed.

01:23:44.400 --> 01:23:45.660
You laughed?

01:23:45.840 --> 01:23:52.460
Yes. I used to play with you
when you were four years old.

01:23:52.460 --> 01:23:54.360
Did you forget?

01:23:54.360 --> 01:23:58.470
It was so unlike the Red Comet
to have allowed Garma to die.

01:23:58.790 --> 01:24:02.520
And when the Flanagan Institute
was first contacted <i>by...</i>

01:24:02.520 --> 01:24:05.290
...the great tactician, Char, it was
natural to think it a bit strange.

01:24:05.290 --> 01:24:09.560
When I realized that deceitful
officer was little Casval...

01:24:09.560 --> 01:24:11.350
...I was more amused than upset.

01:24:12.230 --> 01:24:14.760
Thank you, Lady Kycilia.

01:24:14.760 --> 01:24:19.700
Since I've given you command of my
Newtype Corps, you must be truthful.

01:24:19.700 --> 01:24:23.360
If you've abandoned destroying the
Zabi family and aren't Casval now...

01:24:23.360 --> 01:24:25.580
...what are your
intentions as Char Aznable?

01:24:25.580 --> 01:24:29.910
What happened with Garma...
It felt empty.

01:24:30.950 --> 01:24:35.550
To put it your way, I gained
no satisfaction from revenge.

01:24:35.550 --> 01:24:38.230
It left me feeling empty.

01:24:38.230 --> 01:24:41.050
It seemed funny.
I laughed at myself.

01:24:42.460 --> 01:24:44.260
Similar to my own father.

01:24:44.260 --> 01:24:49.520
If, as my father said, there's to be
a rebirth for man into a Newtype Age,

01:24:49.520 --> 01:24:50.830
I want to see it.

01:24:50.830 --> 01:24:52.270
That's what I'm after.

01:24:54.440 --> 01:24:59.150
I hold no love for Gihren.
Just remember that.

01:25:01.410 --> 01:25:03.650
For the new era!

01:25:05.020 --> 01:25:06.740
Politics can be
complicated at times.

01:25:07.490 --> 01:25:09.040
Quite.

01:25:12.590 --> 01:25:15.880
Man, they've rolled out
another new weapon?

01:25:15.880 --> 01:25:20.400
The Zeon are amazing.
Is this a Newtype-use unit?

01:25:20.400 --> 01:25:23.560
When the Woodward Fleet
contacted it three hours ago...

01:25:23.560 --> 01:25:25.500
...they also picked
up that “Ia-la" sound.

01:25:25.500 --> 01:25:30.240
So, this tulip-looking, tricorn hat
thing was broadcasting it?

01:25:30.810 --> 01:25:32.640
You think it's Char in this?

01:25:33.750 --> 01:25:35.810
That's not the problem.

01:25:35.810 --> 01:25:39.350
How do we beat something that destroys
you before you can detect it?

01:25:39.350 --> 01:25:42.150
And how do we destroy
this Tricorn Hat?

01:25:42.150 --> 01:25:45.530
Get real! Does the book say how
to handle this? I bet not!

01:25:46.590 --> 01:25:50.250
The Zeon are 10 years
ahead of the Federation!

01:25:50.250 --> 01:25:54.290
We have to maximize our
advantages and just survive.

01:25:54.290 --> 01:25:56.620
Can't I just go home
and be nice to my parents?

01:25:57.670 --> 01:26:00.250
That's fine, assuming all
you're after is survival.

01:26:00.970 --> 01:26:03.800
That's not what I meant!

01:26:03.800 --> 01:26:09.350
I don't feel like falling on my sword for
a bunch of useless Fed officers!

01:26:09.350 --> 01:26:14.910
Kai has a point, but our
real enemy is the Zabi family.

01:26:14.910 --> 01:26:17.750
And after they're gone,
do we fight the Federation, too?

01:26:17.750 --> 01:26:18.430
Huh, Sayla?

01:26:20.690 --> 01:26:23.290
I never had a head for politics.

01:26:23.290 --> 01:26:25.820
All I really understand
is fighting for your freedom.

01:26:26.500 --> 01:26:29.630
Pretty vague reason for a
brainy person like you, Sayla.

01:26:29.630 --> 01:26:32.280
What's wrong
with it being vague?

01:26:32.280 --> 01:26:33.660
What do you mean, Newtype?

01:26:34.310 --> 01:26:38.430
Well, no one really understands
what Zeon Deikun meant...

01:26:38.430 --> 01:26:40.810
...when he talked about
the coming rebirth of man.

01:26:40.810 --> 01:26:45.430
But humans have the ability
to adapt to new environments.

01:26:45.430 --> 01:26:48.110
And there are always those who
reject what surpasses themselves.

01:26:48.110 --> 01:26:51.600
That's what we have to fight!

01:26:51.600 --> 01:26:54.330
We'll start by running
right at the enemy fleet.

01:26:54.330 --> 01:26:56.390
I think we should
take out about half.

01:26:56.390 --> 01:26:59.980
Then, under your command,
we'll attack their mobile suits.

01:26:59.980 --> 01:27:01.610
Yes, Captain.

01:27:01.610 --> 01:27:03.860
From here on,
I take orders from you.

01:27:03.860 --> 01:27:05.210
Captain?

01:27:05.210 --> 01:27:08.780
Yes. You're far better
than I am.

01:27:08.780 --> 01:27:10.910
Captain, no, you're...

01:27:10.910 --> 01:27:13.940
You've shown me more than
I could ever teach you.

01:27:13.940 --> 01:27:15.440
Believe in yourself.

01:27:15.440 --> 01:27:16.800
Yes, sir.

01:27:26.260 --> 01:27:27.420
Captain.

01:27:27.960 --> 01:27:31.920
From now on, wear a normal
suit when you go into battle.

01:27:32.970 --> 01:27:35.440
Only because you ask me to.

01:27:35.440 --> 01:27:37.430
Thank you.

01:27:41.940 --> 01:27:44.330
Mobile suit teams launched!

01:27:44.330 --> 01:27:48.200
Attack formation assumed,
with Char's Zanzibar in the lead!

01:27:48.200 --> 01:27:49.440
Excellent.

01:27:50.030 --> 01:27:52.040
The Gwazine will hold here.

01:27:52.040 --> 01:27:54.170
30 seconds after
Captain Char launches...

01:27:54.170 --> 01:27:56.370
...give him 30 seconds
of covering fire!

01:28:04.760 --> 01:28:07.490
We're not gonna lose the
ship we go back to, right?!

01:28:07.490 --> 01:28:08.460
Incoming!

01:28:08.460 --> 01:28:10.490
Right 10 degrees
at half past 1 o'clock!

01:28:19.310 --> 01:28:21.200
Four ships approaching
at 9 o'clock!

01:28:21.200 --> 01:28:21.890
Open fire!

01:28:25.320 --> 01:28:26.230
Don't stop!

01:28:34.230 --> 01:28:36.250
Both sides lost two ships each!

01:28:36.250 --> 01:28:38.910
They'll send in the suits next!
Prep A-A defenses!

01:28:38.910 --> 01:28:42.830
Mobile suits approaching in teams
of 5 and 6! Total number: unknown!

01:28:56.920 --> 01:29:00.010
There? No. I see!

01:29:01.820 --> 01:29:02.600
Below me!

01:29:06.690 --> 01:29:07.850
The Tricorn Hat!

01:29:09.560 --> 01:29:10.320
I see it!

01:29:14.370 --> 01:29:15.960
Other parts of the Tricorn Hat?

01:29:17.240 --> 01:29:18.070
I see them!

01:29:25.480 --> 01:29:28.430
This isn't working!
Find the control lines...

01:29:38.930 --> 01:29:40.120
<i>Got 'em!</i>

01:30:00.110 --> 01:30:01.120
You monster!

01:30:28.560 --> 01:30:31.600
You're too powerful.

01:30:32.250 --> 01:30:34.410
If I don't defeat you,
Char will die!

01:30:34.410 --> 01:30:37.210
<i>Char?! But...</i>

01:30:37.780 --> 01:30:40.410
You came to me too late!

01:30:40.610 --> 01:30:42.260
<i>Too late?</i>

01:30:42.260 --> 01:30:46.330
Why? Why did you
have to show up now?!

01:30:52.130 --> 01:30:55.730
Why do you fight like this?
Why?!

01:30:55.730 --> 01:30:59.660
You have no one!
Nothing to fight for!

01:30:59.660 --> 01:31:01.010
<i>What do you mean?!</i>

01:31:01.010 --> 01:31:02.500
I can see it.

01:31:02.500 --> 01:31:06.690
You have no home, no family!
No one you love!

01:31:06.690 --> 01:31:10.310
But... But...I
What difference does that make?!

01:31:14.980 --> 01:31:18.480
<i>Is it wrong to fight when
you've nothing to fight for?</i>

01:31:18.480 --> 01:31:20.610
<i>It isn't natural.</i>

01:31:20.850 --> 01:31:22.740
<i>Then why do you fight?</i>

01:31:22.740 --> 01:31:26.860
<i>I fight for the
one who saved me.</i>

01:31:28.170 --> 01:31:30.760
<i>Is... Is that all?</i>

01:31:31.100 --> 01:31:34.080
<i>It's a truth
that people live for!</i>

01:31:35.310 --> 01:31:37.960
<i>But, then, what does our
meeting each other mean?!</i>

01:31:42.150 --> 01:31:47.640
<i>Why? Why did I meet you now,
after it's too late?</i>

01:31:47.820 --> 01:31:53.640
<i>If it's fate,
it's a horrible one. Cruel.</i>

01:31:53.860 --> 01:32:00.740
<i>Nothing can come of our
meeting each other. Nothing!</i>

01:32:00.740 --> 01:32:05.460
<i>But this is happening!
You have to accept it!</i>

01:32:05.460 --> 01:32:07.770
<i>And if! do accept it?</i>

01:32:07.770 --> 01:32:11.040
<i>Nothing can come
of our meeting!</i>

01:32:11.280 --> 01:32:12.000
Lalah!

01:32:12.000 --> 01:32:14.710
- Amuro!
- Amuro! No...

01:32:14.710 --> 01:32:17.270
<i>In joining, we now
understand each other.</i>

01:32:17.650 --> 01:32:21.090
<i>Why did I have to
meet you like this?</i>

01:32:21.090 --> 01:32:24.290
<i>When you came to me,
it was too late.</i>

01:32:24.290 --> 01:32:31.590
<i>And for me, it was too soon.
It's always this way for people.</i> ,,

01:32:51.850 --> 01:32:54.210
Lalah! Stop playing
around with him!

01:32:55.050 --> 01:32:55.920
Captain!

01:32:58.490 --> 01:32:59.250
Char!

01:33:01.360 --> 01:33:03.510
The Gundam...
And a red mobile suit!

01:33:11.440 --> 01:33:12.970
Big brother, get out of here!

01:33:19.350 --> 01:33:20.330
Big brother!

01:33:33.660 --> 01:33:34.660
Captain, no!

01:33:34.830 --> 01:33:35.880
What?!

01:33:40.530 --> 01:33:42.000
Artesia...

01:33:47.940 --> 01:33:49.270
Char, prepare to die!

01:33:50.280 --> 01:33:51.180
<i>Captain!</i>

01:33:53.980 --> 01:33:55.390
Lalah!

01:33:55.390 --> 01:33:56.400
<i>Lalah...</i>

01:33:58.620 --> 01:33:59.730
Lalah!!!

01:34:19.270 --> 01:34:23.180
<i>People are changing.
Becoming like us.</i>

01:34:23.180 --> 01:34:26.270
<i>Yeah. You're right, Lalah.</i>

01:34:26.270 --> 01:34:28.950
<i>Do you really believe that, Amuro?</i>

01:34:28.950 --> 01:34:32.600
<i>I do. Because you and I were
able to understand each other.</i>

01:34:32.600 --> 01:34:35.770
<i>Perhaps, someday, people
may even control time itself.</i>

01:34:35.940 --> 01:34:39.880
<i>Oh, Amuro... I can see time!</i>

01:35:46.260 --> 01:35:51.290
I've done something
I can never make right...

01:35:51.930 --> 01:35:56.860
I... I've killed Lalah...

01:36:07.310 --> 01:36:11.610
<i>I can't beat the Gundam.
Not like this. Not now.</i>

01:36:12.450 --> 01:36:16.750
<i>Lalah, show me the way.</i>

01:36:29.840 --> 01:36:33.490
The advance force was
practically wiped out. Terrible.

01:36:33.490 --> 01:36:34.400
<i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

01:36:34.400 --> 01:36:36.930
And you failed to
destroy the Trojan Horse?

01:36:38.010 --> 01:36:42.170
Perhaps I overestimated you.

01:36:42.820 --> 01:36:48.310
<i>Lady Kycilia, special orders from
Commandant Gihren on A Baoa Qu.</i>

01:36:49.120 --> 01:36:53.280
<i>As the Federal Forces continue
to advance on A Baoa Qu...</i>

01:36:53.280 --> 01:36:57.190
<i>...all Zeon ships are to evacuate
the Solar-Ray's firing path!</i>

01:36:57.190 --> 01:36:59.280
<i>Mission time is 21:05.</i>

01:37:00.130 --> 01:37:04.670
He's firing the Solar-Ray in
30 minutes?! It's too soon!

01:37:04.670 --> 01:37:07.120
Damn you, Gihren.
What are you up to?

01:37:07.740 --> 01:37:09.530
Captain, at this rate...

01:37:09.530 --> 01:37:12.170
...we'll never rendezvous
with the main fleet in time.

01:37:12.480 --> 01:37:15.220
Mirai, can the Salamis
to our rear keep up with us?

01:37:16.180 --> 01:37:18.470
Impossible. Let's go on ahead.

01:37:18.470 --> 01:37:20.210
You think that's wise?

01:37:20.210 --> 01:37:24.310
It'll be fine. The Zeon have
cleared out of this sector.

01:37:24.310 --> 01:37:29.120
And there are no more
Newtypes to match Amuro.

01:37:29.120 --> 01:37:31.120
Why do you say that?

01:37:31.660 --> 01:37:36.120
I don't know. Either way, the
White Base will be a little late.

01:37:36.640 --> 01:37:41.900
<i>Meanwhile, the Federation's main fleet,
under the command of General Revil...</i>

01:37:41.900 --> 01:37:48.630
<i>...was gathering at the third
battle line leading to A Baoa Qu.</i>

01:37:49.780 --> 01:37:54.140
<i>It was at this moment that
he revealed their target:</i>

01:37:54.140 --> 01:37:58.620
<i>They would go through
A Baoa Qu and pour into Zeon.</i>

01:37:58.620 --> 01:38:04.280
General. The Great-Degwin
is here to discuss peace terms.

01:38:04.280 --> 01:38:05.550
Sovereign Degwin?

01:38:05.550 --> 01:38:06.790
Yes, sir.

01:38:08.300 --> 01:38:10.300
I see.

01:38:10.300 --> 01:38:13.320
Things are tough
for the Zeon as well.

01:38:28.090 --> 01:38:30.750
<i>But, at that moment...</i>

01:38:31.320 --> 01:38:34.050
This is Gihren on A Baoa Qu.

01:38:34.050 --> 01:38:36.850
I will now give you the
Solar-Ray's final target data.

01:38:36.850 --> 01:38:38.820
Revil's main fleet has
split into three groups...

01:38:38.820 --> 01:38:41.460
<i>...which are attacking
as they advance.</i>

01:38:41.460 --> 01:38:43.860
<i>If we target the Solar-Ray along
the Ge! Dorva firing path...</i>

01:38:43.860 --> 01:38:46.450
<i>...we can take out
half of their fleet.</i>

01:38:46.450 --> 01:38:48.830
<i>Solar-Ray, stand by!</i>

01:38:48.830 --> 01:38:50.130
Roger, sir!

01:38:50.130 --> 01:38:51.560
Solar-Ray, stand by!

01:38:52.480 --> 01:38:54.540
<i>Generator systems: normal!</i>

01:38:54.540 --> 01:38:56.770
<i>Microwave transmitters: normal!</i>

01:38:56.770 --> 01:39:00.630
<i>Output at 85 million
gigawatts per second!</i>

01:39:00.630 --> 01:39:05.180
Firing angle adjustment:
Down 012. Right 0032.

01:39:05.180 --> 01:39:06.790
Primary target: Gel Dorva!

01:39:32.720 --> 01:39:35.440
Attention Musai
at generator panel 825!

01:39:35.440 --> 01:39:37.070
Clear out! Your shadow's
lowering our output!

01:39:43.430 --> 01:39:47.700
Solar-Ray will fire in eight seconds.
Seven... Six...

01:39:47.700 --> 01:39:48.500
Five...

01:39:48.500 --> 01:39:50.470
Four... Three...

01:39:50.470 --> 01:39:51.500
Two...

01:39:51.500 --> 01:39:52.370
One...

01:40:02.520 --> 01:40:05.320
No! Keep us back!

01:40:05.320 --> 01:40:07.570
A whirlpool of light and people...

01:40:07.570 --> 01:40:09.970
They... They're melting!

01:40:11.420 --> 01:40:13.350
The light's pure hatred!

01:40:13.350 --> 01:40:15.210
Amuro, what's wrong?!

01:40:15.210 --> 01:40:16.530
Amuro!

01:40:16.530 --> 01:40:19.130
We can't let the light shine!

01:40:19.130 --> 01:40:20.120
“Light?"

01:40:20.530 --> 01:40:22.520
It looks like Sovereign Degwin.

01:40:23.940 --> 01:40:25.720
Now Gihren is...

01:40:25.720 --> 01:40:27.230
Sovereign Degwin!

01:40:27.230 --> 01:40:27.990
What?

01:40:59.910 --> 01:41:01.360
What's that light?!

01:41:01.360 --> 01:41:04.530
It's coming from
General Revil's main fleet!

01:41:04.530 --> 01:41:08.200
They can't all be gone...
They can't all be gone!

01:41:08.200 --> 01:41:09.200
What's happened?!

01:41:14.320 --> 01:41:17.580
The Solar-Ray's been fired
along the Gel Dorva line!

01:41:17.580 --> 01:41:18.670
Did you hear?

01:41:18.670 --> 01:41:19.880
Yeah.

01:41:19.880 --> 01:41:22.880
Hey! How's the
laser sensor look?

01:41:22.880 --> 01:41:26.250
Yeah, I heard it. Did you?

01:41:26.250 --> 01:41:30.190
What are you doing?!
We're at alert level 2!

01:41:30.190 --> 01:41:31.810
Stop chatting with each other!

01:41:35.670 --> 01:41:41.250
The Great-Degwin's IFF code was
tracked on the Gel Dorva line.

01:41:41.250 --> 01:41:42.210
<i>I'm afraid...</i>

01:41:42.210 --> 01:41:43.570
The Great-Degwin...?

01:41:43.570 --> 01:41:48.050
Yes. And we were tracking it in
the same vicinity as the enemy fleet.

01:41:48.050 --> 01:41:50.570
Was there a report of
it going into battle?

01:41:51.320 --> 01:41:52.840
<i>No, ma'am.</i>

01:41:52.840 --> 01:41:56.080
I see. Maintain surveillance
on their remaining forces.

01:41:56.080 --> 01:41:56.960
Aye I

01:41:56.960 --> 01:42:01.040
The Great-Degwin...? Strange.

01:42:14.050 --> 01:42:17.680
We have eight ships here.
All badly damaged.

01:42:17.680 --> 01:42:18.740
- Fraw Bow!
- Aye, sir!

01:42:18.740 --> 01:42:20.140
What's the Luzal say?

01:42:20.140 --> 01:42:25.240
To stand by while the fleet is
gathered around the White Base.

01:42:25.240 --> 01:42:27.180
No, anything besides that?

01:42:27.180 --> 01:42:30.350
No.
Everyone's really confused.

01:42:30.350 --> 01:42:33.740
Attention, all hands on the White Basel
Stand by at alert level 2!

01:42:34.300 --> 01:42:36.130
Can you make out anything?

01:42:36.840 --> 01:42:38.790
They say it's like they
used a Solar-System.

01:42:38.790 --> 01:42:40.570
A Solar-System?!

01:42:40.570 --> 01:42:42.960
The thing we used at Solomon.

01:42:42.960 --> 01:42:45.360
Although the power
level's totally different.

01:42:45.360 --> 01:42:48.800
<i>White Base!
Signal code Beta Tau!</i>

01:42:48.800 --> 01:42:49.590
Roger!

01:42:50.280 --> 01:42:53.570
<i>My brave and loyal Zeon soldiers!</i>

01:42:53.570 --> 01:42:56.910
<i>Half of the Earth
Federal Forces' fleet...</i>

01:42:56.910 --> 01:43:00.230
<i>...has been blasted to
stardust by our Solar-Ray!</i>

01:43:00.230 --> 01:43:04.570
<i>Its light was the light
of Zeon's righteousness!</i>

01:43:04.570 --> 01:43:10.460
<i>No matter how much power the
Federal Forces may still have...</i>

01:43:10.460 --> 01:43:12.930
<i>...after this fatal blow, they are
nothing but a few pathetic remnants!</i>

01:43:12.930 --> 01:43:15.830
<i>I say now, that so weak a force...</i>

01:43:15.830 --> 01:43:21.710
<i>...could not possibly
defeat us here at A Baoa Qu!</i>

01:43:21.900 --> 01:43:25.240
<i>Humanity, under the
care and guidance of...</i>

01:43:25.240 --> 01:43:27.970
<i>...we Zeon, the chosen,
superior nation...</i>

01:43:27.970 --> 01:43:30.970
<i>...will, at last,
gain immortality!</i>

01:43:30.970 --> 01:43:36.100
If this war drags on,
all mankind may be destroyed!

01:43:36.260 --> 01:43:39.260
We must make the incompetent
minions of the Federation pay!

01:43:39.260 --> 01:43:43.520
We Zeon must arise, for the
sake of all our tomorrows!

01:43:58.580 --> 01:44:02.450
Battalions 2 and 4 will
advance from point N.

01:44:02.450 --> 01:44:05.640
With the Luzal
acting as the flagship...

01:44:05.640 --> 01:44:07.940
...we will advance from point S.

01:44:07.940 --> 01:44:10.250
It's obvious we're
undermanned, isn't it?

01:44:10.250 --> 01:44:12.420
If only we could use
the Solar-System, too.

01:44:12.420 --> 01:44:14.890
I think we're safe.

01:44:15.270 --> 01:44:20.030
I know our objective at
A Baoa Qu has the heaviest firepower,

01:44:20.030 --> 01:44:22.120
but it's also
the most fragile position.

01:44:22.120 --> 01:44:23.620
The operation will work.

01:44:23.620 --> 01:44:25.030
Newtype intuition?

01:44:25.030 --> 01:44:25.760
Yes, sir.

01:44:25.760 --> 01:44:27.650
Ready to synchronize!

01:44:27.870 --> 01:44:34.120
Three, two, one, zero!
The operation has begun!

01:44:34.120 --> 01:44:37.160
Right! All hands,
go to alert level 1!

01:44:37.160 --> 01:44:39.580
In ten minutes, we'll
break through the F line!

01:44:41.160 --> 01:44:42.450
Fraw Bowl

01:44:42.760 --> 01:44:45.080
No matter what happens,
never give up hope!

01:44:45.080 --> 01:44:46.750
It'd be a shame
to die at this point.

01:44:48.100 --> 01:44:51.820
Thanks, Amuro!
I won't give up!

01:44:51.820 --> 01:44:55.570
That's my Fraw!
See you later!

01:44:55.970 --> 01:44:57.590
And don't you do anything crazy!

01:44:57.590 --> 01:44:58.760
Okay.

01:44:58.760 --> 01:44:59.600
You okay?

01:44:59.600 --> 01:45:01.220
Yeah.
I'll be down in a sec.

01:45:03.950 --> 01:45:04.910
You're sure you're all right?

01:45:04.910 --> 01:45:06.310
Sorry I made you worry.

01:45:06.310 --> 01:45:08.010
We're gonna stay in E block!

01:45:08.010 --> 01:45:09.900
Good luck, everyone!

01:45:10.590 --> 01:45:11.510
Where's Hayato?

01:45:11.510 --> 01:45:14.250
Fraw's got him.

01:45:15.560 --> 01:45:17.410
Fine by me.

01:45:17.760 --> 01:45:19.910
That's a dirty laugh.

01:45:20.470 --> 01:45:22.250
Nothing wrong with it.

01:45:22.250 --> 01:45:23.040
<i>Perhaps, but...</i>

01:45:24.170 --> 01:45:26.130
Bye-bye! Good luck!
We believe in you!

01:45:26.130 --> 01:45:27.400
Sure!

01:45:30.540 --> 01:45:34.610
Amuro, was what
you said before true?

01:45:34.610 --> 01:45:36.700
No. If Newtypes
could see the future...

01:45:36.700 --> 01:45:39.400
<i>...we</i> wouldn't
have such a hard time.

01:45:39.400 --> 01:45:44.050
If we hadn't asked Amuro to say that,
everyone might have deserted.

01:45:44.690 --> 01:45:45.880
They're scared.

01:45:45.880 --> 01:45:47.390
Damn right they are.

01:45:47.390 --> 01:45:50.650
Hard as they try,
people can't be gods.

01:46:13.320 --> 01:46:15.470
The enemy's spreading a
beam dampening field towards us.

01:46:15.470 --> 01:46:18.680
Respond with missiles.
Hold the mobile suit units in reserve.

01:46:19.660 --> 01:46:23.420
The carrier Dolos is on schedule.
Hold off for a bit.

01:46:23.730 --> 01:46:27.550
Reroute half of S field's
ships to N field.

01:46:28.030 --> 01:46:31.600
Damned Feddies. They're doing well
even with their main fleet gone.

01:46:31.600 --> 01:46:36.350
Gwazine entering from E field!
I think it's Lady Kycilia.

01:46:36.350 --> 01:46:39.540
Good! Reroute it to N field!

01:46:39.910 --> 01:46:42.570
Strange... What's she up to?

01:46:42.570 --> 01:46:45.160
The number of ships fighting
isn't the number she has.

01:46:53.990 --> 01:46:57.350
Looks like they've sent out all
the new Gelgoog suits we have.

01:46:57.350 --> 01:47:00.070
None left for me, I suppose.

01:47:00.070 --> 01:47:04.760
Why don't you try the Zeong?
Although it is only 80% finished.

01:47:04.760 --> 01:47:05.630
“Zeong?"

01:47:05.630 --> 01:47:09.140
It has a psy-commu system,
similar to the Elmeth's.

01:47:09.140 --> 01:47:11.100
You should be able to use it.

01:47:11.100 --> 01:47:12.480
<i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

01:47:12.480 --> 01:47:16.340
I want you to make up for
our losing the Elmeth.

01:47:16.340 --> 01:47:18.020
<i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

01:47:18.020 --> 01:47:19.950
<i>80% finished?</i>

01:47:26.730 --> 01:47:28.820
Launch all mobile suit teams!

01:47:43.640 --> 01:47:45.200
<i>Magellan-class, destroyed!</i>

01:47:45.200 --> 01:47:48.060
<i>Enemy has launched
mobile suit forces!</i>

01:47:48.710 --> 01:47:51.740
That's it, Dolos! Do your worst!

01:47:51.740 --> 01:47:54.840
Commandant!
Lady Kycilia has returned.

01:47:54.840 --> 01:47:56.100
You're late.

01:47:56.100 --> 01:47:58.010
Forgive me, sir.

01:47:59.420 --> 01:48:01.490
I heard the Elmeth was destroyed.

01:48:01.490 --> 01:48:02.250
Yes, sir.

01:48:02.250 --> 01:48:04.620
It couldn't handle a single Gundam?

01:48:04.620 --> 01:48:06.320
We're going to use the Zeong.

01:48:06.320 --> 01:48:07.460
That unfinished prototype?

01:48:07.900 --> 01:48:10.620
Unless we use someone
we think is a Newtype...

01:48:10.620 --> 01:48:11.910
...we won't beat the Gundam!

01:48:12.160 --> 01:48:14.360
Char, again?

01:48:14.360 --> 01:48:15.940
Dolos moving in!

01:48:15.940 --> 01:48:17.960
Don't be <i>so</i> persistent.

01:48:17.960 --> 01:48:21.570
And where is the Great-Degwin?

01:48:22.150 --> 01:48:23.550
Al Zum City?

01:48:24.750 --> 01:48:27.500
Destroyed. It went
out too far ahead.

01:48:27.500 --> 01:48:31.280
Oh? Did Sovereign Degwin transfer
command to someone else?

01:48:31.620 --> 01:48:34.980
Not very subtle, Kycilia.

01:48:35.490 --> 01:48:38.730
Do you think Father would hand
over the Great-Degwin to anyone?

01:48:38.730 --> 01:48:40.290
No, I don't.

01:48:40.290 --> 01:48:43.190
Well, there's your answer.

01:49:13.770 --> 01:49:15.590
Damn you, Feddie bastard!

01:49:20.840 --> 01:49:23.500
Our forces are unstoppable!

01:49:24.440 --> 01:49:31.120
80%? Don't be stupid!
The Zeong's at 100% capability!

01:49:32.120 --> 01:49:33.910
It doesn't have any legs.

01:49:33.910 --> 01:49:37.990
They're just for show, anyway.
The brass never understand that.

01:49:37.990 --> 01:49:40.810
Unless we use someone
we think is a Newtype...

01:49:40.810 --> 01:49:44.150
A psy-commu, huh?
Think I can handle it?

01:49:44.150 --> 01:49:47.020
Captain, your Newtype
abilities are unknown.

01:49:47.530 --> 01:49:49.250
I can't make any guarantees.

01:49:49.250 --> 01:49:51.700
You speak your mind.
Better watch that.

01:49:51.700 --> 01:49:52.960
Sorry, sir.

01:49:54.040 --> 01:49:57.390
For what it's worth,
I think you'll do fine.

01:49:57.980 --> 01:49:59.570
Thanks. I believe you.

01:50:13.660 --> 01:50:16.730
Ah, the Dolos. It's doing well.

01:50:16.730 --> 01:50:20.450
Then again, the Feddies don't
have enough to beat us here.

01:50:20.450 --> 01:50:23.730
A new fleet?! Federal Forces?!

01:50:24.040 --> 01:50:25.430
What?

01:50:25.430 --> 01:50:26.830
Are you certain?

01:50:26.830 --> 01:50:29.930
On the N field perimeter.
I'll <i>assess</i> the size.

01:50:30.240 --> 01:50:32.180
The Feddies are doing quite well.

01:50:32.780 --> 01:50:34.000
You think so?

01:50:34.000 --> 01:50:37.060
Isn't it just the last desperate struggle
of the surviving fleet?

01:50:38.280 --> 01:50:39.870
Of course.

01:50:40.390 --> 01:50:43.220
What's the status
of Captain Char's Zeong?

01:50:43.960 --> 01:50:44.880
<i>Yes?</i>

01:50:44.880 --> 01:50:46.460
How is the Zeong?

01:50:46.460 --> 01:50:47.380
<i>About to move out!</i>

01:50:47.380 --> 01:50:51.320
We've spotted a
new fleet above S field.

01:50:51.320 --> 01:50:54.350
Use the 34th Mobile Suit
Team and take it out!

01:50:54.350 --> 01:50:58.820
<i>Yes, ma'am! We'll take out the
enemy approaching from S field!</i>

01:50:58.820 --> 01:51:02.670
The Feddies shouldn't have
any more forces in reserve.

01:51:04.410 --> 01:51:08.190
Even S field should hold
against this level of force.

01:51:08.190 --> 01:51:10.070
Yes, Commandant.

01:51:13.650 --> 01:51:15.600
<i>You patricidal monster!</i>

01:51:34.770 --> 01:51:36.450
<i>Now, then...</i>

01:51:36.450 --> 01:51:40.870
The question is whether
I can do as well as Lalah.

01:51:52.420 --> 01:51:53.760
Go to hell!

01:52:08.410 --> 01:52:10.160
Up <i>2</i> degrees! Evasive action!

01:52:10.160 --> 01:52:11.030
Aye, sir!

01:52:15.750 --> 01:52:20.410
Excellent! But where is he?!

01:52:22.390 --> 01:52:24.340
There! Mobile suits!

01:52:29.360 --> 01:52:31.010
That big one... Char?!

01:52:32.800 --> 01:52:34.760
From behind?! What them?

01:52:38.200 --> 01:52:41.190
It seems like a stronger
Newtype than Char. But...

01:52:43.480 --> 01:52:47.940
But my real enemy isn't him!
He's in there!

01:52:54.190 --> 01:52:57.780
It seems the Dolos forces
can hold N field by themselves.

01:52:57.780 --> 01:52:59.880
Excellent.

01:53:07.330 --> 01:53:10.660
Father was on
board the Great-Degwin...

01:53:10.660 --> 01:53:15.060
And he was with the
Federation fleet. Why?

01:53:15.060 --> 01:53:16.970
It couldn't be helped.

01:53:16.970 --> 01:53:20.830
What would have come from
mistimed peace negotiations?

01:53:21.710 --> 01:53:25.480
He wouldn't have
been killed, Commandant.

01:53:26.380 --> 01:53:28.340
Stop fooling around.

01:53:28.650 --> 01:53:33.210
You aren't usually
this naive, my brother.

01:53:42.500 --> 01:53:44.630
That's Commandant Gihren!

01:53:45.500 --> 01:53:50.000
Even the Commander in Chief cannot
get away with killing his father!

01:53:50.000 --> 01:53:53.800
Anyone who objects may file
charges after this battle is over!

01:54:01.050 --> 01:54:03.880
Record that Commandant Gihren
died gloriously in battle!

01:54:03.880 --> 01:54:05.430
Lady Kycilia, your orders?

01:54:06.860 --> 01:54:09.370
Twanning... Thank you.

01:54:09.370 --> 01:54:11.750
As of now, I am assuming
command of A Baoa Qu!

01:54:11.750 --> 01:54:14.330
Dispatch mobile suit
units to N field!

01:54:14.330 --> 01:54:16.030
What's the situation
in S field?!

01:54:16.030 --> 01:54:19.260
Yes, ma'am! Ten of the twenty-
five ships are destroyed!

01:54:19.260 --> 01:54:21.910
The rest are holding
on in S field!

01:54:23.280 --> 01:54:25.790
<i>Send Char's Zeong out in front!</i>

01:54:28.380 --> 01:54:31.540
Concentrate mobile suit
forces in S field!

01:54:44.230 --> 01:54:44.970
<i>Let's go!</i>

01:54:48.930 --> 01:54:49.940
Who's next?

01:54:52.470 --> 01:54:54.270
These new models are good!

01:54:58.910 --> 01:55:00.710
I wonder what's wrong, Mirai.

01:55:00.710 --> 01:55:03.580
Momentarily,
their defenses weakened.

01:55:04.080 --> 01:55:07.310
You're right.
Something strange happened.

01:55:07.310 --> 01:55:10.870
We're not doing well,
but then neither are they.

01:55:11.990 --> 01:55:12.790
So it seems.

01:55:20.220 --> 01:55:23.500
This is pathetic!
I lost the Gundam!

01:55:23.500 --> 01:55:24.720
Damn it! Where is it?!

01:55:27.570 --> 01:55:32.100
Their mobile suits are breaking
through in N field as well.

01:55:32.540 --> 01:55:34.550
I'm getting worried.

01:55:34.550 --> 01:55:35.840
Chen's Zeong?!

01:55:35.840 --> 01:55:38.400
The enemy units are keeping
him away from the Gundam!

01:55:39.420 --> 01:55:41.370
He's still not
used to the Zeong!

01:55:45.990 --> 01:55:48.080
All right!
They've broken through!

01:55:50.130 --> 01:55:53.540
Char! He's found me!

01:55:55.970 --> 01:55:58.390
I see you!
I see you, my enemy!

01:56:00.970 --> 01:56:05.590
Why are our Gelgoogs and Doms
maneuvering so poorly, Twanning?

01:56:05.590 --> 01:56:09.400
Well... Many of them have
pilot trainees at the controls.

01:56:09.400 --> 01:56:11.330
Students?

01:56:11.330 --> 01:56:14.770
But they've been
fully trained, ma'am.

01:56:17.160 --> 01:56:20.570
I believe you, but the question
is how effective are they?

01:56:20.750 --> 01:56:21.620
They seem too weak.

01:56:21.620 --> 01:56:23.120
I'm sorry.

01:56:23.120 --> 01:56:25.790
But they're all
very patriotic, so...

01:56:26.500 --> 01:56:30.260
I wish Gihren had truly
believed in Newtypes.

01:56:30.260 --> 01:56:32.050
He shouldn't
have been so arrogant.

01:56:33.000 --> 01:56:35.540
We'll destroy the enemy one
by one inside of A Baoa Qu!

01:56:35.540 --> 01:56:39.000
There aren't that
many of them left!

01:56:41.260 --> 01:56:43.180
Why do you have
to come at me?!

01:56:48.190 --> 01:56:50.680
<i>F- Fire...! Mother!</i>

01:57:00.230 --> 01:57:01.250
Gotcha!

01:57:05.000 --> 01:57:06.240
He dodged it?!

01:57:15.950 --> 01:57:17.110
Char!

01:57:22.450 --> 01:57:24.810
Maria!!!

01:57:26.880 --> 01:57:29.120
Intensify starboard firepower!

01:57:29.120 --> 01:57:30.810
The GM squadron appears to
have broken through!

01:57:30.810 --> 01:57:32.770
One more battalion
and they'll all be in!

01:57:32.770 --> 01:57:34.230
Right!

01:57:34.470 --> 01:57:37.260
Fraw Bowl Where are
our Guncannons?!

01:57:37.260 --> 01:57:40.310
Intact! They've broken
through to S point's main gate!

01:57:42.320 --> 01:57:44.190
I can't let Kai
do all the work!

01:57:46.340 --> 01:57:48.990
Bastards!
We were here first!

01:57:53.080 --> 01:57:57.330
Real stupid. Times like this make
me glad I'm a natural coward!

01:58:04.500 --> 01:58:05.840
Gundam!

01:58:09.200 --> 01:58:12.530
From this close you can't use
that four-way attack, Char!

01:58:13.170 --> 01:58:14.290
What?!

01:58:14.290 --> 01:58:16.400
Why did you drag
her into this?!

01:58:16.400 --> 01:58:18.900
Lalah never should have
been sent out to fight!

01:58:24.050 --> 01:58:25.670
Char!

01:58:35.560 --> 01:58:37.790
Come on!
Don't die on me, man!

01:58:39.580 --> 01:58:42.290
Leave the rest to
the mobile suit teams!

01:58:46.270 --> 01:58:48.920
That Gundam pilot, “Amuro”...

01:58:48.920 --> 01:58:52.500
How do I beat
a Newtype like him?!

01:58:54.150 --> 01:58:56.810
Tell me, Lalah...
Tell me what to do!

01:58:59.650 --> 01:59:01.480
Portside engine,
emergency shutdown!

01:59:02.690 --> 01:59:04.820
- Eject engine pod, Mirai!
- Aye!

01:59:09.290 --> 01:59:10.290
Moving in for landing.

01:59:10.290 --> 01:59:11.910
Go to it. To all hands:

01:59:11.910 --> 01:59:13.720
Prep for land battle!
Hand-to-hand combat!

01:59:13.720 --> 01:59:15.060
Aye, sir!

01:59:17.540 --> 01:59:18.910
I've lost helm control!

01:59:38.420 --> 01:59:40.510
Both of the White Base's
engines are out!

01:59:43.230 --> 01:59:45.110
What about everyone on board?!

01:59:46.160 --> 01:59:49.020
It's dangerous here!
Take the kids and get out!

01:59:49.020 --> 01:59:50.440
Aye, sir!

01:59:50.440 --> 01:59:51.990
- Don't forget sidearms!
- Aye, sir!

02:00:11.960 --> 02:00:12.980
Wrong spot!

02:00:14.160 --> 02:00:15.340
Gundam!

02:00:19.360 --> 02:00:20.350
Damn you, Char!

02:00:23.940 --> 02:00:26.930
I'm not dead yell He just
took out my main camera!

02:00:26.930 --> 02:00:29.530
<i>Zeong, destroyed!
Cancel IFF code!</i>

02:00:29.530 --> 02:00:30.930
<i>No response from N field!</i>

02:00:30.930 --> 02:00:33.400
The Red Comet
has fallen as well?

02:00:34.610 --> 02:00:37.770
<i>W field, block 24:
send us some ammo!</i>

02:00:38.950 --> 02:00:44.050
But, if the Gundam pilot has
developed unusual Newtype abilities...

02:00:44.050 --> 02:00:46.910
...then it was unavoidable.
Don't you agree?

02:00:46.910 --> 02:00:48.250
Yes, Excellency.

02:00:52.400 --> 02:00:55.620
You're to surrender this position
15 minutes after I escape.

02:00:55.620 --> 02:00:57.260
But...!

02:00:57.260 --> 02:01:01.160
We still have our forces
at Granada and in the Principality!

02:01:01.160 --> 02:01:05.430
But, escape at this point
will be difficult at best...I

02:01:05.430 --> 02:01:09.000
As long as I live,
Zeon will not vanish.

02:01:10.920 --> 02:01:13.620
And what happens to
me after we surrender?

02:01:13.620 --> 02:01:16.250
You'll be brought home
when we exchange POWs.

02:01:16.250 --> 02:01:17.440
Now prepare my ship.

02:01:17.440 --> 02:01:18.280
At once!

02:01:22.330 --> 02:01:24.040
They're like ants! Everywhere!

02:01:27.030 --> 02:01:28.720
Enemy ground troops
are coming out!

02:01:28.720 --> 02:01:31.290
All hands, hold them off
with bazookas and rifles!

02:01:38.680 --> 02:01:43.240
Even Char has to understand who
we should really be fighting!

02:01:46.820 --> 02:01:48.270
He's here.

02:02:28.130 --> 02:02:32.660
Straight ahead leads into the heart
of A Baoa Qu! I can do this!

02:02:32.660 --> 02:02:37.200
Lalah may have been the one
who gave you all your power.

02:02:37.200 --> 02:02:39.470
You should be grateful.

02:02:39.470 --> 02:02:41.740
You're the one who
dragged her into this war!

02:02:43.780 --> 02:02:47.410
If you're saying that's
unforgivable, you're wrong, Amuro.

02:02:48.350 --> 02:02:49.490
What?!

02:02:49.490 --> 02:02:53.270
If not for this war, Lalah's Newtype
abilities never would have awakened.

02:02:53.270 --> 02:02:54.950
That's an excuse!

02:02:54.950 --> 02:02:57.880
No, just the
correct point of view.

02:02:58.110 --> 02:03:00.220
Any closer and I'll shoot!

02:03:00.960 --> 02:03:04.350
You don't understand just
how dangerous you really are.

02:03:04.350 --> 02:03:07.320
You've shown all too clearly
what a true Newtype is.

02:03:07.670 --> 02:03:09.440
And what's
wrong with that?!

02:03:10.700 --> 02:03:15.360
People should accept their limits...
That's why I must kill you!

02:03:43.600 --> 02:03:46.760
That idiot! How am I
supposed to fight by myself?

02:03:57.320 --> 02:03:59.440
Guess it's hand-to-hand, now.

02:04:05.360 --> 02:04:06.480
<i>The others...</i>

02:04:17.960 --> 02:04:20.880
We're not going out to die!
Send some escort units!

02:04:21.970 --> 02:04:23.530
- This is taking too long.
- I'm sorry...

02:04:23.530 --> 02:04:26.950
Just hurry! And don't let
any other soldiers know!

02:04:26.950 --> 02:04:29.870
The company commander
in block 24 is...!

02:04:31.930 --> 02:04:34.520
The ground war's begun?

02:04:34.520 --> 02:04:35.400
That way...

02:04:40.790 --> 02:04:42.890
Because you're
their greatest fighter!

02:04:42.890 --> 02:04:45.150
But our real enemy's
the Zabi family, right?!

02:04:45.150 --> 02:04:47.320
Not to me!

02:04:48.230 --> 02:04:50.620
Do you understand why
I've lured you in here?!

02:04:50.620 --> 02:04:52.620
Because you thought that,
even though I'm a Newtype...

02:04:52.860 --> 02:04:55.710
<i>...I</i> can't use my body any
better than a normal person!

02:04:56.770 --> 02:05:00.760
Even Newtypes need training
to use their bodies well!

02:05:00.760 --> 02:05:02.420
Another excuse!

02:05:07.150 --> 02:05:10.510
Stop it, Amuro!
Stop it, big brother!

02:05:10.510 --> 02:05:12.640
You're the last two people
who should be fighting!

02:05:12.640 --> 02:05:15.390
Stop it, please!
You mustn't fight!

02:05:35.780 --> 02:05:38.210
Just now, Lalah said it!

02:05:38.210 --> 02:05:40.630
“Newtypes aren't tools
for killing each other!"

02:05:41.220 --> 02:05:45.940
All people use Newtypes for now
are as tools for killing each other!

02:05:45.940 --> 02:05:47.970
Lalah was doomed to die.

02:05:48.690 --> 02:05:51.640
And you...
You call yourself a Newtype?!

02:05:51.640 --> 02:05:53.820
You have to stop!

02:06:00.060 --> 02:06:02.610
Amuro! Are you okay?!

02:06:03.240 --> 02:06:05.960
- Artesia!
- Big brother, stop it!

02:06:05.960 --> 02:06:08.780
You have no
reason to hate him!

02:06:08.780 --> 02:06:10.140
He killed Lalah.

02:06:10.140 --> 02:06:12.620
You're both responsible!

02:06:13.520 --> 02:06:16.860
Then join me!
Lalah would want it that way!

02:06:16.860 --> 02:06:18.680
- Are you insane?!
- Big brother!

02:06:18.680 --> 02:06:20.950
I can't just leave
you running wild!

02:06:29.500 --> 02:06:32.690
Big brother,
your forehead's hurt

02:06:32.690 --> 02:06:34.810
If it weren't for my helmet,
I'd have died instantly.

02:07:04.400 --> 02:07:08.150
I was helping
Lady Kycilia escape...

02:07:08.150 --> 02:07:13.430
I... I tried to defend her, but...
Captain, would you...?

02:07:13.430 --> 02:07:17.770
Don't worry. I'll take care
of Lady Kycilia for you.

02:07:18.520 --> 02:07:21.140
<i>Thank you, sir...</i>

02:07:27.860 --> 02:07:31.850
The air here's getting thin.
You'd better escape, Artesia.

02:07:31.850 --> 02:07:34.070
What are you going to do?

02:07:34.070 --> 02:07:37.260
“Grab the opportunities life hands you."
That's my motto.

02:07:37.840 --> 02:07:39.430
Big brother...

02:07:39.430 --> 02:07:43.790
You're an adult now.
It's time to stop playing war.

02:07:44.540 --> 02:07:46.890
Survive and become a fine woman.

02:07:47.240 --> 02:07:48.300
Amuro's calling you.

02:07:49.580 --> 02:07:51.070
Amuro?

02:08:07.300 --> 02:08:08.390
Where's Lady Kycilia?

02:08:08.390 --> 02:08:09.780
She should be leaving port!

02:08:11.900 --> 02:08:15.100
Salamis approaching from above!
Emergency launch, full combat speed!

02:08:15.100 --> 02:08:17.790
Anyone who isn't sitting,
get down on the floor!

02:08:18.040 --> 02:08:20.080
Ten... Nine...

02:08:20.080 --> 02:08:23.030
An offering to you, dear Garma.

02:08:23.550 --> 02:08:25.940
I hope you'll get along
well with your sister.

02:08:25.940 --> 02:08:27.420
Char?

02:08:52.780 --> 02:08:53.760
No good...

02:08:56.980 --> 02:09:00.870
I can't get back to the others.
Even if I could...

02:09:04.020 --> 02:09:06.290
Even if I survive...
My brother is...!

02:09:14.630 --> 02:09:18.100
Damn it...
Is this the end?

02:09:24.910 --> 02:09:26.770
There's still a chance!

02:09:41.660 --> 02:09:45.150
But, what about
everyone on the White Base?

02:09:45.150 --> 02:09:46.820
And Sayla!

02:10:00.410 --> 02:10:03.060
Maybe I should go
to where Lalah is.

02:10:03.060 --> 02:10:06.510
<i>Newtypes shouldn't
kill each other, right?</i>

02:10:06.510 --> 02:10:09.970
<i>Right... What should</i> I <i>do?</i>

02:10:12.890 --> 02:10:16.150
<i>You and I can enjoy
ourselves anytime.</i>

02:10:17.960 --> 02:10:22.060
I see them, Lalah...
I see them all!

02:10:35.750 --> 02:10:38.010
<i>You can see.</i>

02:10:40.220 --> 02:10:43.610
Sayla! Get up! Please get up!

02:10:44.990 --> 02:10:49.850
Amuro?! Is that you'?!
But I don't know where I am!

02:10:54.100 --> 02:10:55.980
Straight this way?

02:11:01.310 --> 02:11:06.330
<i>Right. Straight for 500 meters,
then turn left 90 degrees.</i>

02:11:07.110 --> 02:11:09.300
500 meters...

02:11:10.780 --> 02:11:12.240
Seal hatch #16!

02:11:12.240 --> 02:11:13.650
Aye, sir!

02:11:13.650 --> 02:11:15.040
Amuro?

02:11:17.590 --> 02:11:20.820
If I don't give the order to
abandon ship, we'll all die!

02:11:20.820 --> 02:11:23.450
Seal the hatch! We don't have
any more friendlies there!

02:11:23.450 --> 02:11:24.880
Aye, aye!

02:11:26.060 --> 02:11:27.590
Amuro?!

02:11:29.900 --> 02:11:32.190
Right, I'll get the Launches
ready to go.

02:11:35.370 --> 02:11:36.730
Amuro?

02:11:36.730 --> 02:11:41.610
<i>Dear, sweet, Fraw...
When the gunfire lets up, run.</i>

02:11:41.610 --> 02:11:44.300
Amuro? But where are you?

02:11:44.300 --> 02:11:47.370
<i>Just get to the Launches. Okay?</i>

02:11:48.250 --> 02:11:51.780
When I run,
you run, tool Okay?

02:11:56.160 --> 02:11:58.590
Dammit, why do they just
have to pick on the White Base?!

02:11:58.590 --> 02:12:01.150
Well, we're son
of an obvious target!

02:12:02.800 --> 02:12:03.990
Did you just hear that?

02:12:03.990 --> 02:12:06.040
<i>Yeah. Amuro...</i>

02:12:06.040 --> 02:12:07.600
He told us
to get out of here.

02:12:07.600 --> 02:12:08.890
I think so.

02:12:09.610 --> 02:12:11.790
The Federal Forces are
probably about to attack.

02:12:11.790 --> 02:12:15.330
If we're winning,
I'd say we can leave.

02:12:15.330 --> 02:12:17.110
<i>Let's go!</i>

02:12:23.490 --> 02:12:24.710
The White Base!

02:12:31.830 --> 02:12:33.580
Sayla! Over here!

02:12:33.580 --> 02:12:35.020
Sayla!

02:12:35.730 --> 02:12:36.590
Kai!

02:12:36.590 --> 02:12:38.380
Okay, we've got her!
Let's go!

02:12:38.540 --> 02:12:40.020
Aye, sir!

02:12:49.010 --> 02:12:50.650
The White Base...

02:12:50.650 --> 02:12:52.730
The White Base is going down.

02:13:12.600 --> 02:13:14.430
If Amuro hadn't warned us...

02:13:14.430 --> 02:13:16.500
...we would have been
caught in that inferno.

02:13:20.980 --> 02:13:25.590
Wait, Amuro isn't
on this Launch! Bright!

02:13:26.380 --> 02:13:27.830
No, he's not.

02:13:27.830 --> 02:13:29.930
Sayla, you and Mirai both
heard him most clearly.

02:13:31.660 --> 02:13:34.150
Sayla, you're an orphan of Zeon.

02:13:34.150 --> 02:13:36.810
Your Newtype abilities are
probably stronger than ours.

02:13:36.810 --> 02:13:38.710
Try to find Amuro!

02:13:39.200 --> 02:13:41.990
<i>But, how...?</i>

02:13:43.130 --> 02:13:44.810
I don't know how to!

02:13:44.810 --> 02:13:48.390
Arnuro's the only one not here!
Can't you find him?!

02:13:48.390 --> 02:13:50.330
Well, <i>but...</i>

02:13:50.330 --> 02:13:53.660
You heard Amuro before,
didn't you?

02:13:54.010 --> 02:13:59.330
I could hear him until I was back at
the White Base, but now... Amuro...!

02:14:21.540 --> 02:14:26.760
People shouldn't sacrifice
themselves just to <i>be...</i> convenient.

02:14:26.760 --> 02:14:29.850
Okay! I know
where he is! I know!

02:14:29.850 --> 02:14:31.870
- Okay, a little to the right!
- Kikka!

02:14:31.870 --> 02:14:34.070
Yeah, a little to the right!

02:14:34.070 --> 02:14:36.040
Okay, there! Go straight!

02:14:36.040 --> 02:14:37.610
What's wrong with you three?

02:14:37.610 --> 02:14:40.380
This way! This way!
You're doing fine!

02:14:40.380 --> 02:14:42.920
You're almost out!

02:14:42.920 --> 02:14:43.590
Amuro!

02:14:43.760 --> 02:14:46.910
They know! But, where?!

02:14:46.910 --> 02:14:49.820
Okay, Amuro? In five...

02:14:49.820 --> 02:14:50.890
<i>Four...</i>

02:14:50.890 --> 02:14:51.830
<i>Three...</i>

02:14:51.830 --> 02:14:52.690
Two...

02:14:52.690 --> 02:14:53.720
One...

02:14:53.720 --> 02:14:54.890
Zero!

02:15:15.390 --> 02:15:16.910
Amuro!

02:15:18.830 --> 02:15:20.120
The others...?!

02:15:51.030 --> 02:15:56.930
Forgive me... I still have
a place to go back to.

02:15:56.930 --> 02:15:59.660
Nothing feels as good as this!

02:16:00.270 --> 02:16:02.910
Please understand, Lalah.

02:16:02.910 --> 02:16:07.140
I can go to be with you anytime.

02:17:04.270 --> 02:17:08.570
<i>On this day,
in the year U. C. 0080...</i>

02:17:09.170 --> 02:17:11.360
<i>...at the conclusion
of this battle...</i>

02:17:11.360 --> 02:17:15.700
<i>...an armistice was
finally signed between...</i>

02:17:15.700 --> 02:17:18.490
<i>...the Earth Federation government
and the Republic of Zeon.</i>

